WEBVTT

00:02.990 --> 00:05.950
Why don't you come to the planetarium?

00:05.950 --> 00:13.100
The beautiful twinkling of eternity
that will never fade, no matter what.

00:13.100 --> 00:18.660
All the stars in the sky await you.

00:57.020 --> 01:00.080
The foolish war of man

01:00.080 --> 01:04.940
has covered the world in ice and steered it towards certain demise.

01:04.940 --> 01:09.470
It's said that the human population is only 100 000.

01:09.470 --> 01:13.500
No one has kept any statistics for a long time.

01:13.500 --> 01:19.850
It's impossible to know the real number.

01:22.280 --> 01:25.180
Step by step...

01:25.180 --> 01:30.080
It's become harder to move my body as I wish.

01:30.080 --> 01:34.220
With every year my load has become
heavier and heavier.

01:34.220 --> 01:40.950
Part of me feels my time has come.

01:41.500 --> 01:45.460
But I still have one task to complete.

01:46.250 --> 01:50.920
Something that's not just my own problem.

01:51.550 --> 01:53.340
So...

01:59.280 --> 02:05.220
I have to tell someone about it no matter what...

02:14.690 --> 02:16.220
Levi!

02:16.220 --> 02:17.640
Job!

02:17.640 --> 02:18.740
Ruth!

02:23.000 --> 02:25.340
Geez, where did they go...

02:25.340 --> 02:27.640
We always tell them they can't stay out for long.

02:27.640 --> 02:29.170
I told you so.

02:29.170 --> 02:32.030
At that age, they never listen.

02:32.030 --> 02:34.110
Isaiah! This is a big problem!

02:34.110 --> 02:35.510
I know.

02:36.030 --> 02:38.270
Anyway let's check around the windmills.

02:38.270 --> 02:40.010
They must be hiding somewhere.

02:40.550 --> 02:41.960
You're right.

02:41.960 --> 02:44.240
We need to finish quickly.

02:44.240 --> 02:46.560
We don't know when the storm will come back...

02:46.560 --> 02:47.770
Jeremiah

02:48.390 --> 02:50.400
We have the northern mill.

02:50.400 --> 02:51.240
Come with me.

02:51.240 --> 02:55.320
Yes!

03:06.400 --> 03:08.720
They went towards the windmills.

03:08.720 --> 03:09.390
Yep.

03:09.390 --> 03:10.600
Did they see us?

03:10.600 --> 03:11.920
Is this really okay...

03:11.920 --> 03:13.080
What are you saying?

03:13.080 --> 03:14.500
We all agreed on it.

03:16.760 --> 03:18.280
Job, be careful!

03:18.280 --> 03:19.420
There could be holes!

03:19.420 --> 03:21.800
It's fine! It's fine!

03:22.720 --> 03:25.930
See, told you so.

03:27.340 --> 03:29.530
Are you okay?

03:29.530 --> 03:30.940
Hey! Stop it!

03:43.660 --> 03:46.830
The storm yesterday must have been really strong.

03:47.420 --> 03:51.080
I've never seen the northern mill so damaged.

03:51.230 --> 03:53.920
They'll be mad if we don't help fix it, won't they?

03:53.920 --> 03:54.410
Yeah.

03:54.410 --> 03:58.120
It's too late now. We said we'd play when we got outside.

03:58.120 --> 03:59.090
Yes, but...

03:59.090 --> 04:02.090
Why do you think we hid from Jeremi...

04:04.510 --> 04:05.610
Ouch...

04:05.610 --> 04:06.970
I tripped again.

04:07.260 --> 04:10.680
How have you tripped twice already?

04:13.190 --> 04:16.110
Job, sorry, move your legs.

04:16.110 --> 04:17.020
Wha!?

04:18.900 --> 04:20.250
What is this?

04:20.250 --> 04:21.480
It's wood.

04:21.480 --> 04:24.950
There seems to be more of it though.

04:25.100 --> 04:26.700
Let's dig!

04:35.640 --> 04:38.140
Hey... This is...

04:38.140 --> 04:38.790
Yeah...

04:39.480 --> 04:40.950
It's a person.

04:40.950 --> 04:41.590
Yeah...

04:41.990 --> 04:44.130
Why is he buried out here?

04:44.220 --> 04:45.740
Don't ask me!

04:45.740 --> 04:47.370
Job, tell the adults.

04:47.370 --> 04:50.120
What!? But they'll know that we..

04:50.120 --> 04:52.420
This isn't the time for that!

04:52.420 --> 04:53.350
Come on, hurry!

04:53.530 --> 04:56.810
Got it!

04:57.510 --> 05:00.560
Do you think he's still alive?

05:00.560 --> 05:01.570
Well...

05:01.980 --> 05:04.570
Ah! His Mask is moving a bit.

05:04.570 --> 05:05.440
He's breathing.

05:05.440 --> 05:06.070
You're right.

05:06.380 --> 05:08.120
Good, he might be okay.

05:16.280 --> 05:17.880
What is.. this?..

05:26.210 --> 05:34.020
~ STARGAZER ~

05:40.200 --> 05:41.320
Are you awake?

05:42.890 --> 05:44.750
Am I...?

05:44.750 --> 05:47.570
Do you remember what happened?

05:48.110 --> 05:52.000
You were found unconscious nearby.

05:52.000 --> 05:53.930
I remember...

05:53.930 --> 05:56.930
I got caught in a blizzard and collapsed.

05:56.930 --> 05:59.170
You shouldn't get up yet.

05:59.680 --> 06:03.260
No, I'm alright.

06:03.260 --> 06:05.720
You really helped me.

06:05.720 --> 06:07.680
Thank you very much.

06:08.270 --> 06:12.380
You saved... my life.

06:12.380 --> 06:13.430
This is...

06:14.520 --> 06:17.230
This is a shelter built just before the great war.

06:18.380 --> 06:22.540
It was built below a church in the desert but later abandoned.

06:22.540 --> 06:26.470
We have been using it as a settlement for several years.

06:26.470 --> 06:30.950
Our last adult man died some time ago.

06:31.160 --> 06:35.910
Now there are only about twenty of us awaiting extinction.

06:37.180 --> 06:39.190
Here, this will warm you up.

06:39.190 --> 06:41.440
Thank you.

06:41.440 --> 06:42.650
Jeremiah.

06:42.650 --> 06:43.880
You may go.

06:43.880 --> 06:47.390
Go and tell the children that he has woken up.

06:47.390 --> 06:49.630
Yes, they'll be very glad.

06:49.970 --> 06:51.820
So warm.

06:51.820 --> 06:54.330
As if I'm really coming back to life.

06:54.330 --> 06:57.640
You don't look very well.

06:57.810 --> 07:00.940
What brings you to these forgotten lands?

07:00.940 --> 07:05.590
You don't look like a scavenger.

07:05.590 --> 07:06.650
Indeed.

07:07.770 --> 07:13.390
There is something I've been searching for for a long time

07:13.390 --> 07:19.000
I was told someone had seen it in a village around this area.

07:19.000 --> 07:24.670
Getting through the mountains wasn't fun
for an old man like me...

07:25.350 --> 07:26.420
But...

07:26.860 --> 07:29.920
Even if I don't find what I'm searching for

07:30.250 --> 07:33.930
I didn't want to have any regrets.

07:35.470 --> 07:36.430
Oh?

07:36.640 --> 07:39.810
It's rare to see you praying.

07:40.000 --> 07:42.600
We were asking the goddess for help.

07:42.600 --> 07:46.230
So that she can help that man.

07:47.800 --> 07:50.060
It came true then, I guess.

07:50.060 --> 07:53.490
The man you found just woke up.

07:54.490 --> 07:57.240
Really, Jeremiah!?

07:58.020 --> 08:01.280
The settlement of Elublanka was destroyed.

08:01.280 --> 08:03.250
That was four years ago.

08:03.640 --> 08:05.400
Is that so...

08:05.400 --> 08:08.640
There is little trade to be done in this region.

08:08.640 --> 08:12.280
No merchants have appeared here for ten years.

08:12.280 --> 08:19.870
If you know about the circumstances in any other settlement, would you mind telling me?

08:19.870 --> 08:25.340
This land is not overly polluted by radiation,

08:25.340 --> 08:28.960
but DNA mutation effects can be seen everywhere.

08:28.220 --> 08:29.540
Hey! Don't push me!

08:28.960 --> 08:32.360
You're right, this place is no exception.

08:29.540 --> 08:32.360
Tss! Be quiet!

08:33.690 --> 08:38.990
Nevertheless, the children are a great treasure to us.

08:38.990 --> 08:40.890
Levi, Job, Ruth.

08:40.890 --> 08:43.820
Stop eavesdropping there and come in.

08:43.820 --> 08:45.110
See, she heard you.

08:45.110 --> 08:46.670
Job, you're too loud!

08:46.860 --> 08:49.170
Oh my...

08:51.490 --> 08:54.860
I was told you were the ones who saved me.

08:54.860 --> 08:57.010
You have my gratitude.

08:57.010 --> 08:58.430
Thank you.

08:58.750 --> 09:03.800
Ezra always says that we
should help those in need.

09:03.800 --> 09:05.390
Were did you come from?

09:05.390 --> 09:07.850
Another village? Somewhere far away?

09:07.850 --> 09:10.150
Well...

09:10.150 --> 09:12.320
I come from very far away.

09:13.170 --> 09:18.160
I have been traveling for a long, long time.

09:18.420 --> 09:22.200
I've been all over the world.

09:22.200 --> 09:23.750
Wow...

09:23.750 --> 09:26.850
Does that over there pique your interest?

09:26.850 --> 09:28.580
Yes.

09:28.580 --> 09:31.340
Is that some kind of bomb?

09:31.340 --> 09:34.420
No, it's nothing dangerous like that.

09:34.860 --> 09:38.430
It's a device that shows you the stars.

09:38.900 --> 09:39.850
Stars?

09:41.970 --> 09:45.280
Tell me, are you the "Stargazer"?

09:45.280 --> 09:46.100
M-m?

09:47.810 --> 09:48.600
Yes.

09:48.720 --> 09:50.500
Oh!

09:50.500 --> 09:54.760
I've heard rumors about you when I was young.

09:54.760 --> 09:58.580
It was my dream to meet you!

09:58.580 --> 10:02.200
To think my dream would true at this age.

10:03.240 --> 10:05.490
Ezra, what's a "Stargazer"?

10:05.490 --> 10:06.800
What does "stars" mean?

10:06.800 --> 10:10.910
Oh, you've never heard about stars?

10:10.910 --> 10:12.710
I don't think so.

10:13.180 --> 10:15.710
Is that so. Well, that's too unusual.

10:16.720 --> 10:22.000
When I was young, I haven't known them either.

10:22.000 --> 10:24.730
I struggled just to survive.

10:24.730 --> 10:28.140
I had no time for stars.

10:28.970 --> 10:31.260
Perhaps it because I met those children

10:31.260 --> 10:35.030
Or perhaps it was because of the reason I'd come to this place.

10:35.910 --> 10:39.750
I was reminded of my meeting with her.

10:39.750 --> 10:45.410
The place where I met her was a sarcophagus city.

10:57.210 --> 11:00.130
Dammit, what a persistent bunch!

11:00.670 --> 11:03.720
Anti-personnel tanks protect the city from intruders,

11:03.720 --> 11:06.940
long after the city itself turned into nothing but rubble and ruin.

11:27.700 --> 11:29.330
A military installation?

11:51.420 --> 11:53.670
I was searching

11:53.670 --> 11:56.810
for preserved foods,

11:56.810 --> 11:58.280
medical supplies,

11:58.280 --> 11:59.800
precision tools,

11:59.800 --> 12:02.840
weapons, ammunition, and so on.

12:02.840 --> 12:04.280
Anything I could use.

12:05.120 --> 12:08.410
That was the job of those
who called themselves Junkers.

12:35.460 --> 12:37.110
Working electricity? Here?

12:39.070 --> 12:42.150
This place doesn't look military.

12:56.310 --> 12:58.170
Congratulations!

12:58.170 --> 13:02.380
You are our 2,500,000th customer!

13:13.710 --> 13:15.450
What the hell is a girl doing in a place like this?

13:18.570 --> 13:19.820
What do you want?

13:20.970 --> 13:22.640
I apologize.

13:22.640 --> 13:25.770
I humbly, humbly apologize.

13:25.770 --> 13:27.530
I was being quite dishonest..

13:27.530 --> 13:34.300
To be precise, you are the 2,487,288th customer.

13:34.300 --> 13:37.710
Actually, that's not entirely accurate either.

13:38.330 --> 13:42.460
Some time ago, I made an exception

13:43.160 --> 13:46.180
and let a little boy and little girl in

13:46.180 --> 13:49.680
when they didn't have enough for the admission fee.

13:50.320 --> 13:57.840
So technically, you are the 2,487,290th customer.

13:57.840 --> 14:00.610
I sincerely apologize...

14:07.280 --> 14:08.820
Um, Mr. Customer?

14:09.700 --> 14:15.250
You are our first customer
in exactly 29 years and 81 days.

14:15.250 --> 14:20.570
Welcome to the rooftop planetarium
of the Flowercrest Department Store!

14:20.570 --> 14:21.720
Are you a robot?

14:21.720 --> 14:23.210
Yes! I am a robot.

14:23.610 --> 14:29.020
My name is Hoshino Yumemi and I am a member of the staff at this institution.

14:33.900 --> 14:35.280
What the hell is that?

14:35.280 --> 14:39.440
It is a bouquet. Please accept this in commemoration of your visit here.

14:42.430 --> 14:44.120
A bouquet, huh?

14:44.120 --> 14:46.110
My apologies!

14:46.110 --> 14:50.190
I was not able to acquire real flowers for you.

14:50.190 --> 14:54.120
The flower shop on the first floor has not answered the telephone for a while.

14:55.580 --> 14:57.870
So I tried making one myself.

15:00.500 --> 15:01.790
Are you broken?

15:03.550 --> 15:06.570
Yes. I am just a little broken.

15:06.570 --> 15:10.430
There currently exists an unidentified
bug in my self-diagnostic subroutines.

15:10.960 --> 15:14.930
My backup CMOS battery is depleted
and must be replaced.

15:15.370 --> 15:19.810
My cervical vertebral power unit is past
its operational lifespan and must be replaced.

15:19.990 --> 15:23.360
There also exists known issues with my personal
information databases

15:23.360 --> 15:25.130
and my conversation subroutines.

15:25.700 --> 15:28.990
Because of them, the tendency to engage in verbose conversation

15:28.990 --> 15:32.720
without taking time into consideration has become a unique characteristic of this unit

15:33.100 --> 15:34.190
You gotta be kidding me...

15:34.190 --> 15:36.200
Um, Mr. Customer?

15:37.960 --> 15:41.820
Are you perhaps not feeling well?

15:41.820 --> 15:44.880
May I escort you to our
department store's medical office?

15:44.880 --> 15:45.960
Mr. Customer? Mr. Customer?

15:46.750 --> 15:47.960
Shut up.

15:47.960 --> 15:50.430
I'm neither a customer, nor am I sick.

15:50.430 --> 15:51.380
Is that so?

15:52.390 --> 15:56.270
Well then, the next projection
will begin in seven minutes.

15:56.270 --> 15:59.290
Please take a seat and wait patiently until then.

15:56.790 --> 15:59.290
Does this thing ever shut up?

15:59.290 --> 16:01.480
Let me repeat myself. I am <i>not</i> a customer.

16:01.960 --> 16:03.060
Is that so?

16:03.060 --> 16:04.510
But since you are here anyway,

16:04.510 --> 16:06.510
by all means, please view the projection.

16:06.510 --> 16:07.470
Shut up.

16:07.470 --> 16:10.050
The projection is only 45 minutes long.

16:10.050 --> 16:11.210
Look, just shut up.

16:11.210 --> 16:14.620
Oh, and I am most sorry,
but smoking during the projection is...

16:13.730 --> 16:15.650
Shut up! Keep your mouth shut!

16:15.730 --> 16:17.810
Please, just stop talking!

16:17.810 --> 16:19.870
Understood. Request acknowledged.

16:20.240 --> 16:21.630
My god.

16:21.630 --> 16:27.450
Um, Mr. Customer. There is one request
I would like to make before I stop talking.

16:27.450 --> 16:29.900
Hey, your silence lasted for only three seconds.

16:31.150 --> 16:33.530
If it is not too much trouble, please take this.

16:36.100 --> 16:38.570
I would like you to view the special projection,

16:38.570 --> 16:41.180
reserved in commemoration of the 2,500,000th customer.

16:41.270 --> 16:42.270
How about it?

16:44.490 --> 16:46.030
Do whatever you want.

16:46.030 --> 16:47.690
Thank you very much.

16:47.690 --> 16:53.990
Well then, I shall go prepare the projection,
so please be patient.

16:54.590 --> 16:55.160
Wait a sec.

16:55.600 --> 16:56.860
Yes?

16:56.860 --> 16:59.220
Is there something I can help you with?

16:59.220 --> 17:01.040
What are you going to show me?

17:01.040 --> 17:02.720
A holovid?

17:02.720 --> 17:03.660
The starry sky.

17:06.290 --> 17:07.920
That is correct. The starry sky.

17:11.230 --> 17:13.300
The starry sky, huh?

17:23.860 --> 17:25.310
I've only got two left...

17:27.820 --> 17:30.010
What?

17:31.490 --> 17:39.020
Thank you all for coming to Flowercrest
Department Store's rooftop planetarium today.

17:39.020 --> 17:44.320
My name is Hoshino Yumemi,
and I am a member of staff at this institution.

17:44.320 --> 17:48.670
Before the projection begins,
I would like to announce a few important things.

17:49.180 --> 17:55.650
Please do not talk or whisper during the projection,
as this would be a disturbance to the other customers.

17:53.730 --> 17:55.650
Maybe if I dry this, I can still use it...

17:55.650 --> 18:01.610
Please turn off your cell phones and any alarms now.

18:01.610 --> 18:08.400
In addition, please do not eat, drink,
or smoke at any time during the projection.

18:08.750 --> 18:14.530
And finally, I would like to
introduce a most important partner
who will take you all into the world of the stars.

18:15.140 --> 18:18.520
Everyone, please welcome her
with a warm round of applause!

18:18.520 --> 18:19.360
Miss Jena!

18:25.180 --> 18:27.040
To tell you the truth...

18:27.550 --> 18:30.460
Miss Jena is...

18:30.730 --> 18:34.800
the name of this big machine!

18:40.230 --> 18:42.410
Um, Mr. Customer?

18:42.410 --> 18:45.780
You are supposed to laugh here.

18:45.780 --> 18:48.860
You expected me to laugh?

18:48.860 --> 18:50.650
Just start already.

18:51.260 --> 18:52.920
Thank you.

18:52.920 --> 18:56.900
I am very grateful
that you are anticipating it this much.

18:57.250 --> 18:59.180
Anticipating, my ass...

18:59.180 --> 19:07.260
Now then, without further ado,
Miss Jena will greet you all!

19:13.790 --> 19:16.460
And once again.

19:16.910 --> 19:20.720
Miss Jena will greet you all!

19:26.480 --> 19:29.020
I thought you were gonna show me the stars.

19:29.500 --> 19:32.010
Um, Mr. Customer... I apologize.

19:32.010 --> 19:34.650
I sincerely, sincerely apologize!

19:36.890 --> 19:38.650
I am ashamed to be telling you this,

19:39.240 --> 19:44.180
but it seems that our projector
is in a state of serious breakdown.

19:44.180 --> 19:47.660
Mr. Manager and the rest of the staff are on a trip,

19:48.080 --> 19:51.800
and a simple unit such as myself
could not possibly grasp the situation...

19:56.070 --> 19:57.800
Whatever.

19:57.800 --> 19:59.170
I don't give a damn.

20:08.560 --> 20:14.350
Do you know what the most irritating thing
is when venturing into that sarcophagus city?

20:19.760 --> 20:24.750
The most irritating thing in that sarcophagus city...

20:24.750 --> 20:28.640
was, without a doubt, the time I met that robot.

20:28.640 --> 20:35.100
Even if it talks to you, don't respond to it.

20:43.090 --> 20:44.490
Just the bouquet.

20:44.490 --> 20:46.260
Gave me a heart attack.

20:47.180 --> 20:54.100
The beautiful twinkling of eternity
that will never fade, no matter what.

20:54.100 --> 20:58.560
All the stars in the sky await you.

20:58.560 --> 21:02.360
Why don't you come to the planetarium?

21:02.360 --> 21:04.160
Good afternoon, Mr. Customer.

21:04.160 --> 21:06.190
How are you feeling?

21:06.190 --> 21:08.700
Been worse. I just fell asleep, is all.

21:09.650 --> 21:12.700
I guess I have about an hour before sunset...

21:14.860 --> 21:18.910
Mr. Customer, you must love the stars.

21:18.910 --> 21:20.430
What makes you think that?

21:20.430 --> 21:23.490
You are wearing a pendant with a constellation design.

21:23.660 --> 21:25.840
That is Cygnus, the Swan.

21:26.550 --> 21:27.010
This?

21:29.270 --> 21:31.640
I'll be going now. Sorry to bother you.

21:32.030 --> 21:33.210
Mr. Customer?

21:33.210 --> 21:36.670
If you wait 18 more minutes,
the next projection will begin.

21:36.670 --> 21:39.150
That device is broken though, right?

21:40.900 --> 21:44.590
That device? Do you mean Miss Jena?

21:44.590 --> 21:45.740
Yeah.

21:45.740 --> 21:48.390
Yes, Miss Jena is currently out of order.

21:48.390 --> 21:52.640
But I expect repairs to be done,
if you wait for just a short while.

21:53.040 --> 21:55.600
Sorry, waiting's not my strong suit.

21:55.600 --> 22:00.800
In that case, how about shopping in our department
store while repairs are being conducted?

22:00.800 --> 22:03.880
There are some great discount
coupons I can print out for you.

22:06.240 --> 22:09.890
There's no one here. Who the hell's gonna fix that piece of junk?

22:10.240 --> 22:12.120
There is no reason for concern.

22:12.120 --> 22:14.730
I have already put in a request for the repair team.

22:14.730 --> 22:18.190
They should be here soon,
and will begin repairs immediately.

22:18.720 --> 22:20.640
I guess she doesn't understand sarcasm...

22:20.640 --> 22:26.430
Um, Mr. Customer? Could it be that you are not feeling well?

22:26.430 --> 22:28.910
If that is the case, I can escort you to the medical—

22:28.910 --> 22:31.290
Enough.

22:31.290 --> 22:37.410
Pardon me for asking,
but what do you mean by "enough"?

22:37.410 --> 22:38.710
I mean, I get it.

22:39.370 --> 22:40.580
I'll be downstairs.

22:40.580 --> 22:42.240
Call me when your repairs are done.

22:42.240 --> 22:44.040
Yes, understood.

22:44.040 --> 22:46.320
So much trouble just to get out of here...

22:46.320 --> 22:47.570
Thank you very much.

22:47.570 --> 22:50.300
I am glad to hear that.

22:50.830 --> 22:55.050
To tell you the truth, I was quite worried
since I thought that you had become displeased

22:55.050 --> 22:58.480
because I made a careless mistake.

22:59.240 --> 23:04.080
We robots take joy in serving

23:04.080 --> 23:06.250
humans and putting you at ease.

23:06.250 --> 23:08.240
We're happy when we're doing it well!

23:09.130 --> 23:14.700
When the projector is repaired, I will broadcast
the news over the building's PA system.

23:17.650 --> 23:20.830
We have a special projection
prepared just for you,

23:21.240 --> 23:24.910
so please don't hesitate to
remind me upon your return.

23:24.910 --> 23:26.050
Sure.

23:26.050 --> 23:29.720
You will be the first customer
to view the special projection.

23:30.340 --> 23:32.120
Every member of our staff gave

23:32.120 --> 23:35.160
their best effort to produce it,

23:35.160 --> 23:38.730
so I too, will perform my role
in this without a single mistake.

23:38.730 --> 23:44.760
Additionally, I will keep your bouquet
safe with the utmost care as well.

23:44.760 --> 23:48.670
I shall patiently await your return.

23:55.070 --> 24:00.080
I don't even know why I'm doing this.

24:00.290 --> 24:06.100
What I do know is that,now that the sun has set,
venturing out is dangerous.

24:06.100 --> 24:11.590
Also, this primitive contraption
is a lot more complex than it looks.

24:12.940 --> 24:18.480
Mr. Customer, how long do you estimate it will take
for your repairs on Miss Jena to be complete?

24:18.480 --> 24:20.350
Hell if I know. Ain't got a clue.

24:20.810 --> 24:24.750
Will it be fixed in time for
tomorrow's 11:00 am projection?

24:24.750 --> 24:26.540
I highly doubt it.

24:26.540 --> 24:30.360
If that is the case, may I put out a notice that
tomorrow's projections will be postponed?

24:30.810 --> 24:32.150
Do whatever you want.

24:32.150 --> 24:33.280
Acknowledged.

24:33.280 --> 24:37.080
I will register
this as a critical directive.

24:37.080 --> 24:37.900
Hey...

24:37.900 --> 24:40.730
This light bulbs' filament is burned out.

24:40.730 --> 24:41.660
Is there a spare—

24:41.660 --> 24:42.710
Mr. Customer.

24:43.160 --> 24:47.500
I apologize for the inconvenience,
but it is almost midnight.

24:47.500 --> 24:52.630
As per protocol,
I will be switching into sleep mode.

24:54.000 --> 24:56.340
The reboot from sleep mode is scheduled for 9:00am.

24:56.750 --> 25:01.260
Remaining operation time
after reboot will be 75 hours.

25:01.260 --> 25:03.350
Well then, good night.

25:03.690 --> 25:05.150
Hey, wait...

25:10.270 --> 25:11.150
God damn it.

25:32.590 --> 25:33.890
Mr. Customer.

25:39.570 --> 25:41.910
Good morning, Mr. Customer.

25:41.910 --> 25:43.560
Were you the one calling me?

25:43.560 --> 25:44.060
Yes, sir.

25:45.730 --> 25:47.060
I was dreaming.

25:47.380 --> 25:49.390
Oh, how wonderful!

25:49.390 --> 25:50.820
Was it pleasant?

25:51.310 --> 25:52.510
Not at all...

25:52.510 --> 25:57.370
As I am a robot, I am incapable of dreaming.

25:57.370 --> 26:01.640
But how shall I put it?
I have very much longed to experience it!

26:01.640 --> 26:04.460
Most dreams are not worth longing after.

26:06.270 --> 26:08.830
Is that so?

26:10.040 --> 26:15.560
Wait a sec. So you're saying you're only operational
for one week out of the entire year?

26:15.560 --> 26:16.400
Yes.

26:16.400 --> 26:22.110
For the past 30 years, the quantity of electricity
delivered to this department store has declined sharply.

26:22.110 --> 26:25.810
As per protocol, I have activated my energy-saving mode.

26:26.060 --> 26:34.070
Two days ago at 9:00 am, I became operational
for the first time in 8601 hours.

26:34.630 --> 26:37.570
Just as I happened to be passing through.
Talk about bad timing...

26:37.950 --> 26:43.140
Five days from now, at midnight,
I will return to hibernation mode for recharging.

26:43.140 --> 26:44.830
I see.

26:45.510 --> 26:49.580
To think the emergency power's
still running after all that's happened...

26:49.770 --> 26:54.090
By the way, Mr. Customer, what do you
intend to do with that rainwater?

26:58.480 --> 27:00.490
Drink it.

27:00.490 --> 27:05.010
Unlike you, I'll die if I don't drink water.

27:06.160 --> 27:09.950
If you'd like, I could prepare a beverage for you.

27:09.950 --> 27:10.560
A beverage?

27:11.100 --> 27:15.570
To tell you the truth,
brewing tea is one of my specialties.

27:16.030 --> 27:18.070
Would you like freshly ground coffee?

27:19.070 --> 27:20.070
Coffee, huh...

27:20.830 --> 27:22.960
How about alcohol, then?

27:22.960 --> 27:26.180
I'm talking bottled distilled
liquor with unbroken seals.

27:26.180 --> 27:28.580
It's actually very important to me.

27:28.580 --> 27:29.860
Yes, we have those things.

27:29.860 --> 27:30.700
Really!?

27:30.700 --> 27:31.320
Where!?

27:31.720 --> 27:36.590
Our department store has several vendors
located on B1 that sell high-grade liquor...

27:37.520 --> 27:39.650
Yeah, yeah, I get the idea.

27:39.650 --> 27:41.050
Of course.

27:41.050 --> 27:47.420
In that case, Mr. Customer, may I inquire
about Miss Jena and her current state of repairs?

27:47.420 --> 27:51.310
No change from last night.
I'm still working on it.

27:54.010 --> 27:55.440
I see...

27:55.870 --> 28:00.190
In that case, I will go and announce
the cancellation of today's projection.

28:02.670 --> 28:03.640
Hey, do you have spare light bulbs
stored away somewhere?

28:09.040 --> 28:11.120
Recently, two of the latest 905 series

28:11.440 --> 28:15.630
have been assigned to the
help desk at the main entrance.

28:15.910 --> 28:18.290
Being FT models,

28:18.290 --> 28:21.570
they both have a much
more adult appearance compared to myself.

28:21.570 --> 28:26.260
Their faceplates are quite detailed, and they are able to shed tears.

28:26.670 --> 28:28.590
Tears, huh.

28:28.590 --> 28:30.270
Try turning it on.

28:30.660 --> 28:33.460
Understood.

28:33.460 --> 28:37.130
This one's okay...

28:37.130 --> 28:39.880
So what, you can't shed tears?

28:39.880 --> 28:40.800
Correct.

28:40.800 --> 28:46.750
Tear-generation functionality was first introduced
in the predecessor models, the 9000 series.

28:46.750 --> 28:47.490
I see.

28:47.920 --> 28:52.490
Good for them.

28:52.490 --> 28:53.160
Switch on.

28:53.160 --> 28:54.670
Understood.

28:54.670 --> 28:56.000
This one's busted.

28:56.720 --> 28:58.560
Guess I have two usable ones...

28:58.560 --> 29:02.260
By the way, may I remove this cable now?

29:02.770 --> 29:09.850
This is a shameful emergency measure
that I should not be showing to customers...

29:09.850 --> 29:12.790
Wait a bit longer. I wanna try the motors.

29:12.790 --> 29:14.590
Understood.

29:14.590 --> 29:16.080
By the way, Mr. Customer.

29:16.080 --> 29:17.530
What is it now?

29:17.530 --> 29:21.070
How does shedding tears feel?

29:22.840 --> 29:24.220
Can't really say.

29:24.220 --> 29:26.950
When I'm crying,
I'm usually not thinking very clearly.

29:27.260 --> 29:29.370
Is that so?

29:29.370 --> 29:35.200
I do not know how to put this,
but I would very much like to be able to shed tears.

29:35.200 --> 29:38.960
As I am an Economy Edition model,
I lack that functionality.

29:39.280 --> 29:41.490
It's not such a good thing anyways.

29:41.490 --> 29:42.760
Is that so?

29:42.760 --> 29:46.310
Yeah, no doubt about it.

29:46.310 --> 29:47.700
All righty.

29:47.700 --> 29:50.060
Move the latitude axis upwards,

29:50.060 --> 29:51.150
bit by bit.

29:51.150 --> 29:51.720
Yes, sir.

29:52.280 --> 29:56.980
For your safety, please evacuate from the radius of revolution.

30:20.750 --> 30:26.260
Mr. Customer, might you have an estimated
time of completion for the repairs of Miss Jena?

30:26.510 --> 30:27.640
Who knows?

30:27.640 --> 30:34.400
Do you think it will be in time
for tomorrow's 11:00 am projection?

30:34.400 --> 30:35.400
Dunno.

30:35.400 --> 30:36.640
Feel free to pray to God.

30:36.740 --> 30:41.170
Which god should I pray to, then?

30:41.170 --> 30:42.020
What'd you say?

30:42.140 --> 30:44.670
For instance, there are the ancient Greek gods:

30:44.670 --> 30:47.370
Zeus, Athena, Apollo,

30:47.370 --> 30:50.190
Hermes, Artemis, Demeter,

30:50.190 --> 30:52.130
Poseidon, Hades...

30:52.130 --> 30:53.800
You sure know a lot.

30:53.800 --> 30:55.790
Just pick your favorite or whatever.

30:56.280 --> 30:56.960
Understood.

30:56.960 --> 30:59.920
In that case, I shall pray to Dionysus.

30:59.920 --> 31:01.850
Who the hell is that?

31:01.850 --> 31:03.780
The god of wine and fertility,

31:03.780 --> 31:05.800
also known by his Roman name, Bacchus.

31:06.410 --> 31:10.080
I felt that this god would surely
be most to your liking, Mr. Customer.

31:10.080 --> 31:12.430
Well, you're not too far off...

31:12.430 --> 31:15.560
Pray to your god, not mine.

31:15.910 --> 31:17.990
My god?

31:17.990 --> 31:19.310
The god of robots.

31:22.190 --> 31:27.240
The information you have requested
does not match any entry in my database.

31:27.240 --> 31:28.480
I see.

31:28.480 --> 31:32.400
However, I have found something related.

31:32.400 --> 31:35.140
This is from a meeting we had about the mythological heavens,

31:35.140 --> 31:37.280
which we featured as a special presentation.

31:37.570 --> 31:41.000
I have the file saved as a hologram.

31:44.200 --> 31:47.510
Is there a heaven for robots?

31:47.510 --> 31:50.300
Of course there is! There has to be!

31:50.300 --> 31:51.260
Right, manager?

31:51.260 --> 31:53.520
Ah, yes, that's right.

31:53.520 --> 31:55.740
What is that place like?

31:55.740 --> 31:58.220
Well...

31:58.220 --> 32:02.030
It's free of malfunctions and
batteries never decay!

32:02.030 --> 32:02.500
Right?

32:02.500 --> 32:04.220
Huh? Um, yeah,

32:04.220 --> 32:08.590
and no software bugs
or any need to replace parts, I heard.

32:08.590 --> 32:12.220
You'll be granted all your other wishes too!

32:12.220 --> 32:13.660
Is that so?

32:13.660 --> 32:15.780
Yes, yes.

32:17.010 --> 32:18.290
I see.

32:19.440 --> 32:24.540
The god you're looking for is the one
in that robot heaven. Keep that in mind.

32:24.780 --> 32:25.980
Understood. Critical data registered.

32:28.550 --> 32:32.810
I am very pleased to have learned about this god.

32:32.810 --> 32:37.680
In fact, I have a wish I would like
to ask the god of robots to grant.

32:38.010 --> 32:41.340
A wish?

32:41.340 --> 32:43.190
What could you possibly want?

32:43.960 --> 32:46.980
Well, it is about Heaven...

32:48.050 --> 32:49.340
What is it?

32:49.340 --> 32:52.070
I apologize for the inconvenience,

32:52.490 --> 32:55.300
but it is almost midnight.

32:55.300 --> 33:01.560
As per protocol,
I will be switching into sleep mode.

33:01.560 --> 33:03.210
It's gotten that late already?

33:04.430 --> 33:07.070
Reboot from sleep mode is scheduled for 9:00 am.

33:07.070 --> 33:11.210
Remaining operation time
after reboot will be 60 hours.

33:11.570 --> 33:14.220
Well then, good night.

33:25.350 --> 33:28.100
Why don't you come to the planetarium?

33:28.100 --> 33:33.740
The beautiful twinkling of eternity
that will never fade, no matter what.

33:34.730 --> 33:35.940
All the stars in the sky await...

33:35.940 --> 33:37.740
Hey, I'm done.

33:39.300 --> 33:44.250
Mr. Customer, are you saying that you
have completed your repairs on Miss Jena?

33:44.800 --> 33:46.250
Yeah, that's right.

33:46.920 --> 33:49.420
I've done all I can.

33:53.580 --> 34:00.890
Thank you all for coming to Flowercrest
Department Stores' rooftop planetarium today.

34:01.680 --> 34:06.140
My name is Hoshino Yumemi,
and I am a member of staff at this institution.

34:06.770 --> 34:11.400
Before the projection begins,
I would like to announce a few important things.

34:11.990 --> 34:17.640
Please do not talk or whisper during the projection,
as this would be a disturbance to the other customers.

34:17.640 --> 34:21.620
Please turn off your cell phones and any alarms now.

34:22.460 --> 34:29.170
In addition, please do not eat, drink,
or smoke at any time during the projection.

34:29.710 --> 34:36.500
And finally, I would like
to introduce a most important partner
who will take you all into the world of the stars.

34:36.500 --> 34:39.470
Everyone, please welcome her
with a warm round of applause!

34:43.060 --> 34:44.310
Miss Jena!

34:50.730 --> 34:52.130
To tell you the truth...

34:52.130 --> 34:54.720
Miss Jena is...

34:54.720 --> 35:00.010
the name of this big machine!

35:00.010 --> 35:08.960
Now then, without further ado,
Miss Jena will greet all of you!

35:14.810 --> 35:18.480
Today, our planetarium was visited

35:18.480 --> 35:25.850
by the 2,487,290th visitor since we first opened.

35:25.850 --> 35:29.940
On behalf of all the staff of our establishment,
I offer you our humblest gratitude.

35:31.800 --> 35:37.650
In commemoration of this special occasion,
we have prepared a special projection.

35:40.240 --> 35:43.870
We hope that you will all enjoy it.

35:49.500 --> 35:53.130
On one fine autumn day, it was raining outside.

35:53.130 --> 35:57.350
Rainy days can make you feel a little down.

35:57.350 --> 36:00.670
But please be at ease.

36:00.670 --> 36:05.050
In here, we can summon the Sun whenever we wish.

36:05.470 --> 36:07.470
Here we have our very own Sun.

36:08.050 --> 36:11.020
Slowly, it sets in the western sky.

36:15.860 --> 36:18.300
Ah, here is the first celestial
body to grace our night sky:

36:18.300 --> 36:20.610
Venus, also known as the Evening Star.

36:21.330 --> 36:24.450
Slowly but surely, the sky is growing darker.

36:24.450 --> 36:27.800
This is our signal to go home.

36:27.800 --> 36:34.970
At last, the curtain of night
slowly falls over the vicinity...

36:39.410 --> 36:42.380
This is the starry sky at 8:00 pm tonight.

36:42.810 --> 36:46.460
Crossing the ceiling above you
right now is the Milky Way,

36:46.460 --> 36:50.660
so named by civilizations of old who saw it

36:50.660 --> 36:54.330
as a river of milk flowing through the sky.

36:54.330 --> 36:59.760
Now, if you could focus your attention on
the highest star, the one set at the ceiling of the sky.

36:59.760 --> 37:03.400
That is Deneb, the first magnitude
star of the constellation Cygnus.

37:03.400 --> 37:07.420
Close by are Vega of the constellation Lyra,
and Altair of Aquila.

37:07.420 --> 37:09.770
Together, the three are called the Summer Triangle.

37:10.560 --> 37:13.660
So far, these have all been summer constellations.

37:14.310 --> 37:23.440
Although today has been a very chilly day,
if you turn your eyes upward towards the night sky,
you can still find these final traces of summer.

37:23.440 --> 37:27.850
Now then, shall we turn our attention
to the autumn constellations?

37:27.850 --> 37:32.710
Please look a little east of Deneb.

37:32.710 --> 37:36.050
The winged horse is Pegasus,

37:36.050 --> 37:39.980
and the chained princess is Andromeda.

37:39.980 --> 37:43.520
The autumn constellations are accompanied
by a famous legend.

37:42.540 --> 37:45.150
It's like the stars are drawing me in.

37:43.520 --> 37:45.150
Andromeda is the heroine.

37:47.070 --> 37:54.270
Andromeda was the daughter of the ancient
Ethiopian king Cepheus and his queen, Cassiopeia.

37:54.270 --> 37:58.110
Cassiopeia boasted about
her daughter's beauty so greatly,

37:58.110 --> 38:02.070
she invoked the wrath of Poseidon,
god of the ocean.

38:02.070 --> 38:07.150
Angered, Poseidon sent a giant
sea monster to the shores of Ethiopia.

38:07.150 --> 38:13.130
Ethiopia was devastated by the
tidal wave caused by the sea monster.

38:13.130 --> 38:16.750
Cepheus received an oracle

38:16.750 --> 38:20.130
saying that to calm Poseidon,

38:20.130 --> 38:22.600
he must sacrifice his daughter Andromeda.

38:22.600 --> 38:29.700
Cepheus was torn, but Andromeda
volunteered to sacrifice herself.

38:29.700 --> 38:31.820
Reluctantly, Cepheus set aside his sorrows

38:31.820 --> 38:36.330
and chained Andromeda to a rock by the coast.

38:36.330 --> 38:39.260
As she lay there trembling

38:39.260 --> 38:42.080
all alone, the sea rose up.

38:42.080 --> 38:44.460
The sea monster had appeared,

38:44.910 --> 38:48.470
and it was closing in on Andromeda.

38:48.810 --> 38:53.230
Struggling as she might, the chains would not let go.

38:53.230 --> 38:59.900
"Save me! Somebody save me!"
In her mind, Andromeda desperately called for help.

38:59.900 --> 39:05.030
It was then when the hero Perseus, riding the winged horse Pegasus, arrived.

39:05.460 --> 39:09.340
Perseus was on his way back from his
successful fight against Medusa the Gorgon.

39:09.480 --> 39:12.970
Noticing that something was amiss
with the shore, he moved closer to check.

39:13.400 --> 39:17.920
Right now, in this very world,
she was an omnipotent storyteller,

39:17.920 --> 39:19.750
and the stars were her little garden.

39:20.200 --> 39:25.290
Princesses, heroes, monsters, and gods...
Each and every one of them
bowed devotedly before her,

39:25.290 --> 39:26.910
playing their individual parts in the

39:26.910 --> 39:29.760
unfolding drama with absolute obedience.

39:30.260 --> 39:34.050
And thus did Andromeda and Perseus
become constellations,

39:34.300 --> 39:37.560
living happily ever after in
the autumn sky to this day.

39:41.180 --> 39:44.320
Let us now turn to our special projection.

39:44.720 --> 39:48.280
It is named "The Reverie of Mankind
Spreading Its Wings Into Space"...

39:50.550 --> 39:51.640
What's wrong?

39:51.640 --> 39:53.450
Did something break?

39:53.450 --> 39:55.030
Or could it be...

39:57.430 --> 39:59.120
There's the fuse board.

40:08.480 --> 40:11.890
Mr. Customer, Miss Jena is not responding.

40:11.890 --> 40:15.050
Neither the projectors nor the axes are activating.

40:15.660 --> 40:19.810
What kind of tools will we require
to repair Miss Jena?

40:20.460 --> 40:22.440
The power's... been cut off.

40:22.990 --> 40:27.660
My sincerest apologies, but I do not understand.

40:27.660 --> 40:34.320
Somehow, this facility, by some sort of miracle
received a weak stream of electrical power over the past 30 years.

40:34.940 --> 40:37.470
But that's come to an end.

40:37.470 --> 40:39.450
So, you mean there's a power outage?

40:39.630 --> 40:43.170
In that case, the emergency power
will come online soon enough.

40:43.170 --> 40:46.460
This place has been supplied by said
emergency power the whole time.

40:47.120 --> 40:49.180
We're out of options.

40:49.180 --> 40:51.720
We're out of options.

40:52.280 --> 40:56.660
Um, Mr. Customer,
then does this mean that the special projection...

40:56.660 --> 40:57.700
Listen closely to what I say.

40:59.430 --> 41:01.730
Yes, sir.

41:01.730 --> 41:06.830
Continue the projection.
Your voice alone will suffice.

41:06.830 --> 41:10.350
My sincerest apologies, but I do not understand.

41:10.350 --> 41:12.110
I said, continue.

41:12.960 --> 41:17.240
I don't need the projector. I just want to
hear your explanations and commentary.

41:17.360 --> 41:18.740
Can you do that?

41:18.740 --> 41:20.650
Yes, I certainly can.

41:20.650 --> 41:24.770
But if it is just my commentary alone,
then that will not be a projection.

41:24.770 --> 41:25.460
It's okay.

41:26.200 --> 41:29.180
I know all about the stars already.

41:29.180 --> 41:33.470
I'll be able to understand everything you
want to show me just from you speaking.

41:34.300 --> 41:38.470
You must be very fond of the stars, Mr. Customer.

41:38.910 --> 41:45.550
I am truly honored to have you
as a customer of our humble establishment.

41:45.550 --> 41:46.270
Yeah.

41:46.520 --> 41:51.770
In that case, very well. We will continue
the projection through my explanations alone.

41:51.770 --> 41:55.030
This way, please.

41:56.310 --> 42:00.240
She really is trusting.

42:03.930 --> 42:07.370
I shall now resume the special projection.

42:11.820 --> 42:15.880
A very, very, very long time ago...

42:16.720 --> 42:23.060
Huddled within cold, dark caves, the earliest
forefathers of humanity lived together.

42:24.100 --> 42:30.060
The world was locked in ice, and huge,
tusked beasts still roamed the land.

42:30.780 --> 42:35.900
One long, freezing night, a young man woke up.

42:35.900 --> 42:40.070
Likely due to a combination of the bitter cold
and gnawing hunger, he was unable to sleep.

42:41.250 --> 42:47.790
He rubbed his sleepy eyes, and peered
outside at the entrance of the cave.

42:48.800 --> 42:55.560
Upon the freezing night sky, countless numbers of stars twinkled brightly.

42:55.830 --> 42:58.030
Ever since that day,

42:58.030 --> 43:04.280
mankind has never ceased to gaze up
at the heavens in all its vastness with wonder.

43:09.420 --> 43:16.410
Was there ever any doubt that humanity would set
its sights beyond the sky, towards space itself?

43:16.410 --> 43:18.810
Towards unknown heights?

43:18.810 --> 43:21.090
Breaking free of the darkness of night...

43:21.090 --> 43:23.530
Taking the tears of many,

43:23.530 --> 43:27.900
and forging them into the seeds of new dreams...

43:28.350 --> 43:33.130
And finally, on one fateful day,
those hands reached out into space.

43:33.130 --> 43:39.960
Here is the third planet of the solar system.
Our planet, Earth.

43:39.960 --> 43:43.120
No matter where on Earth you look,
our planet is teeming with beauty.

43:43.120 --> 43:51.360
but currently, there are many disputes, conflicts,

43:51.360 --> 43:52.980
and problems that can't yet be resolved.

43:52.980 --> 43:56.280
Overpopulation, energy, food,

43:56.280 --> 43:59.020
space territoriality.

43:59.020 --> 44:02.380
However, it is my sincere belief

44:02.380 --> 44:05.820
that mankind will be able
to solve all of its problems.

44:05.820 --> 44:10.290
And then, they will reach out
to the heavens above.

44:13.610 --> 44:18.300
On this special night,
I would like to let you in on a big secret.

44:20.770 --> 44:25.430
This planetarium is also a time machine!

44:30.040 --> 44:32.640
It allows us to traverse time at will,

44:33.310 --> 44:38.360
from the distant past into
the furthest reaches of the future.

44:41.670 --> 44:43.380
Please take a look.

44:43.380 --> 44:48.910
This is the starry sky that will be seen precisely
one thousand years from this day, in this very place.

44:49.450 --> 44:55.340
Miss Jena the projector, and I, Hoshino Yumemi
the robot, did our best to construct

44:55.340 --> 44:58.910
this meager starry sky of the future.

44:58.910 --> 45:04.760
Please, everyone, don't forget
the starry sky that you saw here.

45:05.600 --> 45:07.550
If you ever find yourself lost in the darkness,

45:07.930 --> 45:11.800
no longer able to see the real starry sky,

45:11.800 --> 45:14.310
please remember it.

45:15.220 --> 45:16.770
This is... my little reverie.

45:20.670 --> 45:25.600
Well then, let us return to our own day and age.

45:25.600 --> 45:29.950
The celestial spheres are revolving.

45:31.830 --> 45:36.510
The winter constellations are appearing
above the eastern horizon.

45:36.510 --> 45:40.590
Orion, Auriga, Taurus...

45:40.590 --> 45:45.270
These are the harbingers of a magnificent season
that will soon be unfolding every night.

45:45.270 --> 45:50.720
The long night has finally ended,
and morning has once again come to the world.

45:50.720 --> 45:52.970
The sun has risen.

45:52.970 --> 45:57.530
The twittering of small birds and
the rustling of the wind are now audible.

46:00.160 --> 46:06.830
The slumbering buildings and trees, too, are sleepily
opening their eyes to greet the rays of the sun.

46:06.830 --> 46:09.730
Very soon, the town will spring to life,

46:09.730 --> 46:13.200
and just as ever, a new day will begin.

46:13.200 --> 46:15.620
Good morning, everyone.

46:17.520 --> 46:21.200
That marks the end of our special projection.

46:21.200 --> 46:26.710
It has been an honor to have you join me,
Hoshino Yumemi, on this journey.

46:26.710 --> 46:31.180
Thank you for listening so attentively.

46:39.760 --> 46:41.450
Mr. Customer, today's projection is over.

46:41.450 --> 46:44.900
Today's projection is over.

46:45.280 --> 46:47.110
Mr. Customer?

46:50.190 --> 46:52.160
It would seem he has fallen asleep.

46:53.160 --> 46:55.140
After taking all the factors into account,

46:55.140 --> 47:01.250
I think that it would be best to allow
Mr. Customer to sleep like this until morning.

47:06.750 --> 47:08.160
Mr. Customer,

47:08.160 --> 47:10.110
Mr. Manager once told me

47:10.110 --> 47:15.850
that it's a great privilege for a human being
to be able to sleep beneath the starry sky.

47:16.880 --> 47:23.100
This is why I believe that surely, you must have
enjoyed the special projection, Mr. Customer.

47:23.100 --> 47:25.760
That brings me much joy

47:25.760 --> 47:30.560
I wonder what kind of dream you are having?

47:26.380 --> 47:30.560
In this world without any real stars,

47:30.560 --> 47:34.250
I'm a robot and can't have dreams...

47:30.560 --> 47:34.250
the stars she showed that day

47:34.250 --> 47:39.370
are forever with me when I close my eyes.

48:02.500 --> 48:05.320
What is a "Stargazer"?

48:05.320 --> 48:07.400
Is he different from normal merchants?

48:07.740 --> 48:09.630
Well, yeah...

48:09.630 --> 48:11.820
I think he is different.

48:11.820 --> 48:13.910
He doesn't sell anything.

48:14.410 --> 48:16.790
Ezra was very happy.

48:17.260 --> 48:22.140
She kneeled before him like when praying to the goddess

48:22.140 --> 48:27.130
We are honored to have you here, Stargazer.

48:27.520 --> 48:29.580
Really, the chief did?

48:29.580 --> 48:33.880
If only he were a bit younger, you know.

48:33.880 --> 48:36.880
He can't really make children like that.

48:36.880 --> 48:40.140
Stop it, Isaiah! It's not about that!

48:40.420 --> 48:42.460
Hey, Jeremiah...

48:42.460 --> 48:43.690
What's a star?

48:43.690 --> 48:44.560
Eh!?

48:44.560 --> 48:46.820
Well...

48:46.820 --> 48:50.360
Like the Sun, the Moon, and other stuff like that.

48:50.860 --> 48:52.990
The Sun? The Moon?

48:52.990 --> 48:55.030
So he is a person who sells light bulbs?

48:55.340 --> 48:56.680
No.

48:56.680 --> 49:00.460
The Sun isn't a light bulb.
It's something that is outside.

49:00.460 --> 49:04.960
But we went outside a while back,
and we didn't see any sun.

49:04.960 --> 49:07.160
There's nothing like that anywhere.

49:07.160 --> 49:08.920
That's because...

49:09.090 --> 49:10.940
I don't understand.

49:10.940 --> 49:13.050
Where did the come Stargazer from?

49:13.050 --> 49:14.010
From the stars?

49:14.210 --> 49:16.610
No, I don't think so.

49:16.610 --> 49:18.540
The Stargazer is a normal man.

49:18.540 --> 49:21.640
If he's a normal man,
why is he the Stargazer?

49:21.880 --> 49:24.140
Why's he traveling like a merchant?

49:24.140 --> 49:24.960
Hmm...

49:24.960 --> 49:25.940
Why?

49:25.940 --> 49:27.390
Yes, why!?

49:27.390 --> 49:29.720
Isaiah, not you too.

49:29.720 --> 49:30.940
I'm kidding.

49:30.940 --> 49:36.570
I'm telling you I don't have all the answers.

49:36.830 --> 49:39.080
Are you doing your job well?

49:39.080 --> 49:40.570
We are!

49:40.570 --> 49:44.290
Yes! Our best!

49:44.290 --> 49:46.480
Jeremiah, Isaiah.

49:46.480 --> 49:49.740
I hear that our harvest has decreased this again this year.

49:49.740 --> 49:51.340
What about the new fertilization?

49:51.790 --> 49:55.240
The potatoes are growing well, but the vegetables...

49:55.240 --> 49:56.320
I see.

49:56.320 --> 49:58.340
We'll keep trying!

49:58.340 --> 49:59.970
I'm counting on you.

49:59.970 --> 50:01.130
Got it!

50:01.130 --> 50:03.530
Levi, Job, Ruth.

50:03.530 --> 50:04.600
Come with me.

50:04.600 --> 50:05.750
Uh?..

50:05.750 --> 50:09.920
The Stargazer wants to see you.

50:09.920 --> 50:13.550
I have a request for you.

50:13.550 --> 50:15.160
Request?

50:15.160 --> 50:16.940
Do you know what an umbrella is?

50:16.940 --> 50:18.000
Hmm?..

50:18.000 --> 50:21.380
It's something used to protect you
from the rain or the snow.

50:21.380 --> 50:24.040
But maybe that doesn't tell you much.

50:24.040 --> 50:27.460
I've seen a picture of one.

50:28.000 --> 50:33.440
I'd like you to help me make a very big umbrella.

50:33.440 --> 50:36.840
I've lost the one I was using before.

50:37.100 --> 50:38.840
Are you going outside?

50:39.420 --> 50:42.960
No, it's to be used indoors.

50:42.960 --> 50:48.020
Is there a place where no one would mind if we put up a big umbrella?

50:48.240 --> 50:50.060
The hall would be perfect.

50:50.060 --> 50:53.420
Yep, no one will be mad about that!

51:14.400 --> 51:15.920
I can't cut it well.

51:16.140 --> 51:18.520
Yes, that's long enough.

51:18.520 --> 51:21.520
The trick is to make it longer than you need.

51:21.520 --> 51:24.400
Can you tell us what we are making now?

51:24.400 --> 51:26.660
The umbrella, of course, Levi!

51:26.660 --> 51:28.760
He said at that at the start.

51:28.760 --> 51:32.320
He said it was something to protect from rain and snow!

51:32.320 --> 51:35.690
It doesn't rain or snow indoors,

51:35.690 --> 51:37.260
so this isn't an umbrella.

51:37.260 --> 51:38.450
But...

51:40.300 --> 51:41.240
Well...

51:41.630 --> 51:43.240
I see.

51:43.240 --> 51:46.750
Do you want to know what this really is?

51:47.500 --> 51:48.680
Yes!

51:51.070 --> 51:53.400
This is space.

51:53.400 --> 51:54.750
Space?..

51:55.470 --> 51:57.360
To be precise,

51:57.360 --> 52:00.960
it's a model of a part of outer space.

52:00.960 --> 52:06.220
Of course, the real thing isn't this small.

52:06.220 --> 52:09.100
But if it's too big, I can't carry it around.

52:09.100 --> 52:11.770
That's why I only make it this size.

52:11.770 --> 52:13.770
What is space?

52:14.250 --> 52:16.940
It is far, far away beyond the sky,

52:16.940 --> 52:19.150
It's the place where stars are.

52:19.530 --> 52:22.030
How far is far, far away?

52:22.250 --> 52:23.960
Good question.

52:23.960 --> 52:26.280
That is...

52:27.550 --> 52:28.540
Are you okay!?

52:28.600 --> 52:31.540
I... I'll get Ezra!

52:31.880 --> 52:34.670
No... I'm okay.

52:35.310 --> 52:38.320
Um... I'm sorry.

52:38.320 --> 52:42.900
Answering your questions is very fun.

52:42.900 --> 52:48.610
But can I answer that question a bit later?

52:48.610 --> 52:49.930
Yes.

52:50.280 --> 52:51.900
Thank you.

52:51.900 --> 52:55.690
Well then let's continue making the umbrella.

52:56.300 --> 52:58.920
Levi! Ruth! Hurry up!

52:58.920 --> 53:01.780
The umbrella is almost done!

53:01.780 --> 53:03.280
Not so fast, Job.

53:03.280 --> 53:06.360
We still have to work on the fields!

53:06.360 --> 53:09.610
I know!

53:11.040 --> 53:12.080
Did you hear?

53:12.080 --> 53:14.920
He's making the children build something.

53:15.130 --> 53:17.290
Oh, that old man, you mean.

53:17.290 --> 53:20.800
They're using a lot of cloth and such.

53:17.660 --> 53:19.180
What is it, Job?

53:19.180 --> 53:20.800
Shh!

53:21.180 --> 53:25.300
That cloth could have gone to make so many clothes.

53:25.300 --> 53:29.060
It's not just cloth. He's also another mouth to feed.

53:29.160 --> 53:32.860
An old fart who can't make children isn't really good for anything.

53:32.860 --> 53:36.190
If only he was 30 years younger...

53:36.550 --> 53:38.940
That's right!

53:37.360 --> 53:38.940
I'm going down there.

53:39.600 --> 53:40.770
Levi?

53:40.770 --> 53:42.820
Job, don't.

53:42.820 --> 53:43.710
But?

53:43.710 --> 53:47.450
We know the adults have it hard too, right?

53:47.740 --> 53:50.580
But they shouldn't talk about him like that.

53:51.480 --> 53:53.340
You're right.

53:53.340 --> 53:58.460
Ezra always says that we should help those in need.

53:58.970 --> 54:03.460
So why do the adults say things like that?

54:04.160 --> 54:05.710
That's...

54:05.710 --> 54:10.470
I don't know...

54:17.020 --> 54:19.110
It feels weird.

54:19.580 --> 54:25.100
You made a great umbrella for your your first try.

54:25.100 --> 54:28.560
Yes, it's very good.

54:28.560 --> 54:30.110
Levi, Job.

54:30.110 --> 54:33.150
Hang black curtains from the edge of the umbrella,

54:33.150 --> 54:36.700
so that light can't enter.

54:36.700 --> 54:37.870
And then...

54:38.300 --> 54:41.790
We should prepare the device, Ruth.

54:41.960 --> 54:43.300
Eh?

54:43.930 --> 54:49.130
That's it, you can't have too much or too little grease.

54:49.130 --> 54:50.480
Careful.

54:50.480 --> 54:51.300
Got it.

54:51.850 --> 54:52.720
Job!

54:52.720 --> 54:54.650
You can't leave any gaps.

54:54.650 --> 54:56.230
I know.

54:56.400 --> 54:58.160
Are you okay?

54:58.160 --> 54:59.700
We can switch any time.

54:59.700 --> 55:02.160
All okay!

55:02.160 --> 55:05.900
I'm doing it better than you!

55:05.900 --> 55:11.930
A projector is always hard to please,
and it's always in a bad mood.

55:11.930 --> 55:14.490
It is a very sensitive device.

55:14.900 --> 55:18.860
No matter the age or the projector.

55:18.860 --> 55:22.200
You are doing very well.

55:22.200 --> 55:24.080
Really?

55:24.080 --> 55:25.250
Yes.

55:25.250 --> 55:29.860
Now hold and press that spring.

55:29.860 --> 55:31.010
Like this?

55:31.360 --> 55:34.520
Very good.

55:34.520 --> 55:38.840
Now try to continue setting it up using this book.

55:38.840 --> 55:39.520
Eh?

55:39.800 --> 55:40.800
I... Can't do that...

55:42.360 --> 55:44.040
Don't worry.

55:44.040 --> 55:45.880
I'll watch you.

55:45.880 --> 55:47.720
Try it.

55:47.720 --> 55:52.500
Well, since I wrote it by hand,
you might not be able to read it.

55:52.500 --> 55:55.280
My handwriting is not very good.

55:59.150 --> 55:59.960
Yes!

55:59.960 --> 56:01.040
I'll try!

56:02.110 --> 56:06.800
To start the motor and lights, you need to wind it about five minutes.

56:07.320 --> 56:11.230
If it's not enough,
we can charge it partway through.

56:11.230 --> 56:12.280
Ok!

56:12.280 --> 56:13.800
Should I take over?

56:14.250 --> 56:15.350
It's alright!

56:15.350 --> 56:16.470
Leave it to me!

56:17.880 --> 56:21.850
When you're done, we can try it out.

56:37.270 --> 56:39.460
What's that round thing?

56:39.460 --> 56:41.470
It's the Moon.

56:41.470 --> 56:48.630
The biggest and brightest being in the night sky.

56:59.010 --> 57:02.390
This is... stars?..

57:04.120 --> 57:06.540
This is a joke.

57:06.540 --> 57:08.400
It's,

57:08.840 --> 57:10.580
It's just too beautiful!

57:10.580 --> 57:14.180
Yes!

57:16.340 --> 57:21.250
Wh... Why are they lined up so nicely like that?

57:21.890 --> 57:25.300
The stars elsewhere look more scattered.

57:25.300 --> 57:29.000
After taking in the beauty,

57:29.330 --> 57:31.910
they wanted to know more and more.

57:30.050 --> 57:32.890
Look, they're lining up over there too.

57:31.910 --> 57:34.420
I remember.

57:32.890 --> 57:36.380
That looks like Jeremiah when she gets mad.

57:34.420 --> 57:38.670
I'll answer your questions
as best as I can.

57:38.680 --> 57:40.830
Let's take it one by one.

57:40.830 --> 57:43.140
First Levi's question.

57:43.690 --> 57:48.310
Stars that form a pattern are called constellations.

57:48.310 --> 57:52.470
In ancient times people looked at them...

57:56.450 --> 57:59.380
Okay, shall we end here for today?

57:59.380 --> 58:01.460
Please, just a bit more.

58:01.460 --> 58:04.160
Tell us about the stars!

58:04.450 --> 58:05.760
Yeah!

58:05.760 --> 58:09.200
We don't know when we can see it again!

58:09.200 --> 58:11.670
We have to work in the fields tomorrow so...

58:12.250 --> 58:13.730
Don't worry.

58:13.730 --> 58:19.430
Try closing your eyes.

58:20.140 --> 58:27.000
Now imagine the night sky you just saw.

58:36.960 --> 58:38.450
Do you understand?

58:39.420 --> 58:43.450
Once you've seen them, you will never forget.

58:44.060 --> 58:49.710
Stars are like that.

58:50.760 --> 58:52.560
Good night!

58:52.560 --> 58:53.590
Night!

58:53.820 --> 58:57.180
We'll come again!

59:06.830 --> 59:08.140
Are you alright?

59:10.460 --> 59:13.690
Oh, it is you.

59:14.310 --> 59:17.200
Do you want to look at the stars?

59:17.200 --> 59:19.330
At some other time.

59:19.330 --> 59:21.810
When the others are here as well.

59:21.810 --> 59:23.940
What about your cough?

59:23.940 --> 59:26.800
My lungs are not good.

59:26.800 --> 59:28.460
How bad is it?

59:28.800 --> 59:33.400
I'm lucky to have lived this long in a world like this.

59:33.400 --> 59:37.370
To have let me do what I set out to do for so many years,

59:37.370 --> 59:40.090
I'm very grateful for my body.

59:40.960 --> 59:43.850
If only it could hold on for a tiny bit longer.

59:45.120 --> 59:48.750
If you didn't come to look at the stars,
what can I do for you?

59:48.750 --> 59:50.350
That's right.

59:50.990 --> 59:54.860
I thought I could share a small luxury with you.

59:55.980 --> 59:58.360
That's very kind of you.

01:00:03.470 --> 01:00:07.120
It's been a long time!

01:00:07.120 --> 01:00:10.070
They did a good job.

01:00:10.070 --> 01:00:13.190
To think they would work so excitedly.

01:00:13.190 --> 01:00:16.630
They have been raised very well.

01:00:17.340 --> 01:00:20.730
Almost miraculously well.

01:00:20.730 --> 01:00:24.510
Are other settlements that bad?

01:00:25.180 --> 01:00:30.010
Some treat all outsiders as enemies...

01:00:30.010 --> 01:00:34.270
Others think only about breeding...

01:00:34.480 --> 01:00:40.550
Compared to them, this place is orderly and welcoming.

01:00:40.550 --> 01:00:43.110
In such dark times,

01:00:43.110 --> 01:00:46.780
those are the most valuable things you can have.

01:00:47.290 --> 01:00:52.900
Hearing that makes it worth the effort.

01:00:52.900 --> 01:00:59.300
But as you can see there is no future for them in this village.

01:01:01.380 --> 01:01:06.460
Chief, I want to ask something of you.

01:01:06.460 --> 01:01:08.180
What is it?

01:01:09.070 --> 01:01:14.050
Could you leave the children to me?

01:01:14.050 --> 01:01:17.320
I wish to make them my successors.

01:01:19.210 --> 01:01:24.070
They are more qualified to be Stargazers than I.

01:01:24.570 --> 01:01:27.210
Smart, honest, innocent...

01:01:27.210 --> 01:01:32.130
It should also open up a better future for them.

01:01:32.130 --> 01:01:35.830
That's what I believe.

01:01:40.840 --> 01:01:45.490
Tomorrow morning the village will have a meeting.

01:01:45.490 --> 01:01:48.100
I will bring it up then.

01:01:48.620 --> 01:01:50.070
But...

01:01:50.070 --> 01:01:53.250
even if the village accepts,

01:01:53.250 --> 01:01:56.350
ultimately, the children will be the ones to decide.

01:01:56.600 --> 01:01:58.100
Of course.

01:01:58.100 --> 01:02:00.610
Thank you so much.

01:02:07.870 --> 01:02:08.700
Job!

01:02:08.700 --> 01:02:10.490
Wake up, Job!

01:02:11.450 --> 01:02:13.400
We decided yesterday, didn't we?

01:02:13.400 --> 01:02:14.800
Hurry!

01:02:14.800 --> 01:02:16.000
Oh! Right!

01:02:18.830 --> 01:02:19.500
M?..

01:02:19.940 --> 01:02:21.640
Where are you going?

01:02:21.640 --> 01:02:22.490
Jeremiah!?

01:02:22.490 --> 01:02:23.100
Geh!

01:02:23.100 --> 01:02:24.370
What is it!?

01:02:24.370 --> 01:02:26.320
No, nothing.

01:02:26.320 --> 01:02:29.050
You better not be up to something again.

01:02:29.050 --> 01:02:30.650
We're not!

01:02:30.650 --> 01:02:34.710
There's an important meeting soon,
so don't charge off.

01:02:34.710 --> 01:02:37.120
Are we going too?

01:02:37.120 --> 01:02:38.600
Adults only.

01:02:38.600 --> 01:02:41.820
Though they might call your teacher.

01:02:41.820 --> 01:02:42.720
Isaiah!

01:02:43.660 --> 01:02:46.570
Are you going to look at the stars?

01:02:46.800 --> 01:02:49.080
Maybe...

01:02:49.080 --> 01:02:50.070
Levi! Ruth!

01:02:50.350 --> 01:02:51.230
Let's go!

01:02:51.230 --> 01:02:52.410
Yep!

01:02:52.410 --> 01:02:53.580
We'll be back soon!

01:02:53.750 --> 01:02:55.400
Don't go outside!

01:02:55.400 --> 01:02:57.310
Come back soon!

01:02:57.310 --> 01:02:58.670
Got it!

01:03:23.270 --> 01:03:25.030
Hi!

01:03:25.910 --> 01:03:27.360
Oh, it's you.

01:03:27.360 --> 01:03:28.790
Come in.

01:03:28.790 --> 01:03:30.030
Yes.

01:03:31.390 --> 01:03:32.990
We...

01:03:32.990 --> 01:03:35.770
We have a request!

01:03:35.770 --> 01:03:38.040
Oh, what is it?

01:03:40.880 --> 01:03:43.540
We want to become Stargazers!

01:03:45.930 --> 01:03:49.400
I bet Ruth can make the machine.

01:03:49.400 --> 01:03:51.340
You can maintain it too, right?

01:03:51.340 --> 01:03:52.620
Yes!

01:03:52.620 --> 01:03:57.310
And Job can pull the sled when traveling between villages.

01:03:57.710 --> 01:04:03.390
And I can tell everyone about the stars.

01:04:03.390 --> 01:04:07.930
But I don't think I can do it unless I learn more.

01:04:07.930 --> 01:04:08.610
So!

01:04:08.880 --> 01:04:13.740
Please teach us more so
we can become real Stargazers.

01:04:13.740 --> 01:04:17.120
We'll give you this in exchange.

01:04:17.900 --> 01:04:21.250
This is our treasure.

01:04:21.250 --> 01:04:25.930
It may not be enough, but...

01:04:36.640 --> 01:04:39.400
No, not at all.

01:04:39.400 --> 01:04:40.890
This is more than enough.

01:04:41.020 --> 01:04:42.680
Really!?

01:04:42.680 --> 01:04:46.780
But I also have a request for you.

01:04:46.780 --> 01:04:48.510
Request?

01:04:48.510 --> 01:04:49.400
Mm?..

01:04:50.240 --> 01:04:53.910
I want you to take this.

01:04:54.530 --> 01:04:58.710
This is my treasure...

01:04:58.710 --> 01:05:03.680
...A life-changing one at that.

01:05:03.680 --> 01:05:05.670
Why don't you come to the planetarium?

01:05:06.460 --> 01:05:12.890
The beautiful twinkling of eternity
that will never fade, no matter what.

01:05:12.890 --> 01:05:15.140
All the stars in the sky await...

01:05:15.980 --> 01:05:17.970
Good afternoon, Mr. Customer.

01:05:17.970 --> 01:05:19.470
How are you feeling?

01:05:19.760 --> 01:05:22.440
Not particularly good, but not too shabby either.

01:05:22.440 --> 01:05:23.480
I see.

01:05:23.800 --> 01:05:26.640
If you are still feeling ill, by any chance...

01:05:26.640 --> 01:05:28.170
I'm fine.

01:05:28.170 --> 01:05:30.110
I see. I am most relieved to hear that.

01:05:30.820 --> 01:05:37.180
My sincerest apologies for
the breakdown during the projection.

01:05:37.180 --> 01:05:39.240
I beg your pardon
from the bottom of my heart.

01:05:39.900 --> 01:05:41.560
Well...

01:05:41.560 --> 01:05:43.470
Your projection wasn't half bad.

01:05:43.470 --> 01:05:45.170
Your projection wasn't half bad.

01:05:45.830 --> 01:05:48.340
I am overjoyed to hear such a compliment.

01:05:49.010 --> 01:05:53.600
It is also true that you have
helped us out a great deal.

01:05:53.600 --> 01:05:57.300
Say... Just what do you...

01:05:59.770 --> 01:06:00.810
What is it?

01:06:02.260 --> 01:06:04.540
It's nothing.

01:06:04.540 --> 01:06:06.190
I'm heading off now.

01:06:06.190 --> 01:06:07.000
Very well.

01:06:07.000 --> 01:06:09.190
Thank you for everything.

01:06:09.190 --> 01:06:13.150
If you would, send a prayer to the god of robots for me, that I might survive the trip back.

01:06:13.410 --> 01:06:14.560
Certainly.

01:06:32.010 --> 01:06:33.960
Mr. Customer.

01:06:35.920 --> 01:06:39.210
Excuse me, but may I ask you a question?

01:06:39.490 --> 01:06:40.300
What is it?

01:06:40.610 --> 01:06:43.600
Will you be in any danger on your journey home?

01:06:43.860 --> 01:06:46.910
I could say no, but that would probably be a lie.

01:06:46.910 --> 01:06:49.900
Will you be taking the train on your way home?

01:06:50.320 --> 01:06:54.170
The trains aren't running.
There's a power outage right now, remember?

01:06:54.170 --> 01:06:58.650
Then will you be taking a bus or a taxi
or some other kind of vehicle?

01:06:58.650 --> 01:07:01.220
A car, probably.

01:07:01.220 --> 01:07:08.080
Is your car parked within
a three-kilometer radius of here?

01:07:08.080 --> 01:07:10.750
Sounds about right.

01:07:11.470 --> 01:07:14.880
Why are you asking me all this?

01:07:15.520 --> 01:07:21.010
I have sent a request of leave to the support center in order to act on our professional code

01:07:21.130 --> 01:07:23.450
but I am unable to connect.

01:07:23.450 --> 01:07:30.900
As such, I am permitted to act at my own discretion.

01:07:31.570 --> 01:07:34.730
I will escort you to your car, Mr. Customer.

01:07:36.640 --> 01:07:42.030
The duty of escorting the unwell
falls upon us robots.

01:07:43.280 --> 01:07:44.410
Are you crazy?

01:07:45.160 --> 01:07:49.120
No, but I am just a little broken.

01:07:53.320 --> 01:07:55.050
I'm looking at two,
maybe three kilometers by foot.

01:07:55.790 --> 01:07:58.790
How long will your batteries last?

01:07:58.790 --> 01:08:03.480
In my current operational mode,
I can continue for approximately four more days.

01:08:03.480 --> 01:08:05.880
So you'll be able to return without any problems?

01:08:05.880 --> 01:08:06.350
Yes!

01:08:06.990 --> 01:08:07.850
Good. Let's go

01:08:08.410 --> 01:08:09.600
Understood.

01:08:12.360 --> 01:08:15.020
Hey!

01:08:19.800 --> 01:08:23.570
Please watch your step. There is a bump here.

01:08:24.640 --> 01:08:26.680
May I direct your attention here, Mr. Customer?

01:08:26.680 --> 01:08:30.350
The vanilla cream puffs sold
at this store are so popular

01:08:30.350 --> 01:08:32.210
that the queue always
extends well outside the door.

01:08:34.400 --> 01:08:37.610
Do you like cream puffs, Mr. Customer?

01:08:37.610 --> 01:08:40.010
Wouldn't know. Haven't exactly had one before.

01:08:40.320 --> 01:08:44.430
Anyway, I don't need you to be a tour guide,
I need you to pick up the pace. I'm in a hurry.

01:08:44.690 --> 01:08:45.360
Yes,

01:08:45.360 --> 01:08:48.780
understood.

01:08:52.440 --> 01:08:53.710
Mr. Customer,

01:08:53.710 --> 01:08:55.420
located on the fifth floor of this building

01:08:55.420 --> 01:08:57.820
is a beer-hall affiliated with our department store.

01:08:58.300 --> 01:09:00.220
Its menu offers fresh seafood and

01:09:00.220 --> 01:09:02.030
many different kinds of craft beers.

01:09:02.030 --> 01:09:06.700
I'm begging you, cut the chatter
and put that effort into walking faster.

01:09:06.700 --> 01:09:07.380
Yes,

01:09:07.380 --> 01:09:10.310
understood.

01:09:11.590 --> 01:09:11.960
Um,

01:09:12.440 --> 01:09:15.670
Mr. Customer...

01:09:15.670 --> 01:09:16.960
What, need another break?

01:09:17.210 --> 01:09:18.060
Yes.

01:09:18.060 --> 01:09:21.780
My femoral power unit has overheated

01:09:21.780 --> 01:09:23.220
and requires cooling.

01:09:28.920 --> 01:09:31.230
This rain really isn't letting up at all.

01:09:37.760 --> 01:09:38.730
Tell me about it.

01:09:40.000 --> 01:09:44.070
By the way, Mr. Customer,
what is your line of work?

01:09:45.520 --> 01:09:46.240
I'm a Junker.

01:09:47.050 --> 01:09:48.620
Could you elaborate?

01:09:49.360 --> 01:09:52.180
In laymans' terms...

01:09:52.180 --> 01:09:55.080
I'm a garbage collector, I guess.

01:09:55.080 --> 01:09:57.080
Garbage collection?

01:09:57.080 --> 01:10:00.140
That is a very noble profession.

01:10:00.140 --> 01:10:04.670
My body is designed to be completely recyclable...

01:10:04.670 --> 01:10:05.510
About time we got going.

01:10:07.480 --> 01:10:08.180
You good to go?

01:10:08.680 --> 01:10:09.510
Yes,

01:10:09.510 --> 01:10:11.430
let us go on.

01:10:12.130 --> 01:10:13.390
Leave that here.

01:10:14.830 --> 01:10:18.760
By "that" do you mean this bouquet?

01:10:18.760 --> 01:10:19.400
Yeah.

01:10:19.940 --> 01:10:22.680
Holding onto that just makes it
more likely for you to fall over.

01:10:22.680 --> 01:10:25.300
But this belongs to you.

01:10:25.300 --> 01:10:27.910
Look, it's...!

01:10:27.910 --> 01:10:30.220
Fine, I get it.

01:10:30.220 --> 01:10:32.330
The bouquet belongs to me.

01:10:32.330 --> 01:10:34.230
Hand it over.

01:10:34.230 --> 01:10:34.790
Of course.

01:10:37.290 --> 01:10:41.550
Here is your bouquet, Mr. Customer.

01:10:42.350 --> 01:10:45.050
My bouquet, huh?

01:10:50.530 --> 01:10:52.140
A liquor store...

01:10:52.500 --> 01:10:55.640
Mr. Customer, may I ask you something?

01:10:56.060 --> 01:10:59.900
Was this the result of a vehicle collision,
gas explosion, or other accident?

01:11:00.550 --> 01:11:02.540
Could be from combat,

01:11:02.540 --> 01:11:04.280
or a scavenger like me.

01:11:04.280 --> 01:11:06.610
An accident of sorts, I guess.

01:11:10.680 --> 01:11:14.080
Finally found a liquor store
and not a single damn thing's left.

01:11:17.450 --> 01:11:19.330
At least leave half of it standing...

01:11:23.500 --> 01:11:24.090
Wow!

01:11:39.550 --> 01:11:42.290
Is that...!?

01:11:42.290 --> 01:11:46.690
You'd be surprised at how
little it takes to kill a man.

01:11:47.530 --> 01:11:50.620
No wires or a weight-sensitive plate.

01:11:50.620 --> 01:11:52.490
It could also be rigged up with...

01:11:55.160 --> 01:11:55.830
Here you are.

01:12:13.180 --> 01:12:16.060
After all that effort, this is all I get...

01:12:16.370 --> 01:12:18.230
It appears that bottle you
have there is a scotch whiskey.

01:12:18.230 --> 01:12:22.480
A Twelve-year Sherry Barrel...

01:12:22.980 --> 01:12:23.840
Price including tax is...

01:12:23.840 --> 01:12:26.360
You know a lot of things.

01:12:26.360 --> 01:12:27.650
I'm impressed.

01:12:27.650 --> 01:12:30.650
Yes, thank you.

01:12:30.980 --> 01:12:31.880
Mr. Customer,

01:12:31.880 --> 01:12:34.800
is everything all right?

01:12:45.340 --> 01:12:48.060
Mr. Customer.

01:12:48.060 --> 01:12:48.760
There is a bump here, so please watch your step...

01:12:51.770 --> 01:12:54.050
For the fourteenth time...

01:12:54.050 --> 01:12:55.850
I told you to watch where you're going.

01:12:56.440 --> 01:12:58.990
I understand. My apologies.

01:12:58.990 --> 01:13:01.230
I'm surprised you're not in pieces by now.

01:13:01.230 --> 01:13:04.560
I am more durable than
my appearance may suggest.

01:13:05.880 --> 01:13:08.000
That's good to know..

01:13:08.000 --> 01:13:10.490
Yes.

01:13:11.310 --> 01:13:14.070
The streets really are empty.

01:13:14.570 --> 01:13:15.560
Yeah,

01:13:15.560 --> 01:13:16.830
it's just us.

01:13:17.840 --> 01:13:22.870
On rainy days like these,
we can't go outside, so it's very boring.

01:13:23.700 --> 01:13:27.500
However, spending time indoors could be fun too.

01:13:30.770 --> 01:13:33.130
Do you ever get bored?

01:13:33.740 --> 01:13:35.640
Bored? What do you mean?

01:13:36.530 --> 01:13:40.320
You've worked at the planetarium
for a long time, right?

01:13:40.320 --> 01:13:43.230
Haven't you ever wanted to work a different job?

01:13:44.540 --> 01:13:48.060
I am very fond of my job.

01:13:48.060 --> 01:13:52.430
Working with Mr. Manager, the staff,

01:13:52.430 --> 01:13:56.750
and Miss Jena brings me much joy.

01:13:56.750 --> 01:13:57.490
I see.

01:14:00.200 --> 01:14:04.210
Mr. Customer, may I ask you something?

01:14:04.640 --> 01:14:05.800
Hm?

01:14:05.800 --> 01:14:06.460
What is it?

01:14:06.970 --> 01:14:10.630
Have you ever made a wish to your god?

01:14:12.140 --> 01:14:13.910
Perhaps,

01:14:13.910 --> 01:14:15.550
but nothing important.

01:14:16.410 --> 01:14:20.210
Come to think of it, I never asked
you what you would wish for.

01:14:20.210 --> 01:14:21.970
Yes, that is correct.

01:14:22.940 --> 01:14:24.850
What would you wish for?

01:14:26.150 --> 01:14:28.200
Please...

01:14:28.200 --> 01:14:31.770
Please do not divide heaven in two.

01:14:31.770 --> 01:14:35.200
That is my prayer to the god of robots.

01:14:36.610 --> 01:14:40.300
If people and robots were to be
separated at the Gates of Heaven,

01:14:40.300 --> 01:14:43.000
then I would be truly worried.

01:14:43.000 --> 01:14:47.460
Even if I go to Heaven, I still would
like to be of service to all humans.

01:14:47.870 --> 01:14:51.590
I would like to be of assistance
to everyone, now and forever.

01:14:53.670 --> 01:14:54.970
Is that so...

01:14:54.970 --> 01:14:56.630
Yes, it is!

01:14:59.800 --> 01:15:02.720
If I leave her like this, her batteries will run dry.

01:15:03.650 --> 01:15:06.060
If I'm to make her wish come true,

01:15:06.060 --> 01:15:07.980
I would have to take her out of this city...

01:15:08.560 --> 01:15:10.620
But can I force her

01:15:10.620 --> 01:15:13.690
to leave against her will?

01:15:13.690 --> 01:15:17.820
Mr. Customer, is your car still a long way away?

01:15:18.220 --> 01:15:20.120
No, we're nearly there.

01:15:20.590 --> 01:15:22.270
Excellent.

01:15:22.270 --> 01:15:23.830
Shall we continue?

01:15:23.830 --> 01:15:24.490
Yeah..

01:15:26.960 --> 01:15:28.710
It must be

01:15:28.960 --> 01:15:30.960
because I had alcohol for
the first time in ages.

01:15:32.430 --> 01:15:34.550
No...

01:15:34.830 --> 01:15:37.330
I had already been drunk well past my limit

01:15:37.330 --> 01:15:38.760
long before I encountered

01:15:39.280 --> 01:15:41.260
that bottle of whiskey.

01:15:42.180 --> 01:15:43.760
Mr. Customer?

01:15:43.760 --> 01:15:45.350
It's nothing. Let's go.

01:15:47.030 --> 01:15:51.730
What am I going to do with her?

01:16:02.700 --> 01:16:03.790
Mr. Customer,

01:16:03.790 --> 01:16:08.160
these streets are considerably different
from how they show up on my database.

01:16:08.160 --> 01:16:10.840
Have the streets been redeveloped recently?

01:16:10.840 --> 01:16:11.880
It's just as you see.

01:16:12.280 --> 01:16:16.000
Is that a construction machine of sorts over there?

01:16:16.770 --> 01:16:19.330
It's a Fiddler Crab, autonomous fire-support Mech.

01:16:19.330 --> 01:16:21.600
Can you elaborate?

01:16:21.600 --> 01:16:23.510
Something not unlike yourself.

01:16:23.770 --> 01:16:27.390
But here, of all places?
right in front of the quarantine wall?

01:16:28.270 --> 01:16:30.110
Can I make it?

01:16:30.110 --> 01:16:32.980
Mr. Customer?

01:16:32.980 --> 01:16:34.520
I'm going hunting.

01:16:34.520 --> 01:16:37.990
Hunting?

01:16:37.990 --> 01:16:39.990
Stay here until I come back.

01:16:40.740 --> 01:16:43.960
I'm leaving this city soon.

01:16:43.960 --> 01:16:46.740
What will you do after I leave you?

01:16:47.090 --> 01:16:50.750
I will be able to walk back to

01:16:50.750 --> 01:16:52.080
my workplace, so please do not worry.

01:16:52.470 --> 01:16:54.430
There's no one left in this city.

01:16:54.430 --> 01:16:57.060
Even if you were to return,
you'll never again have any customers,

01:16:57.060 --> 01:16:59.270
and you'll never again be able to show
the planetarium to anyone.

01:16:59.270 --> 01:17:02.210
Also, the reactor in this city is on its last legs.

01:17:02.210 --> 01:17:03.800
The projector will never operate again.

01:17:03.800 --> 01:17:06.470
You've seen all of this with your own two eyes!

01:17:07.180 --> 01:17:08.310
Yes,

01:17:08.310 --> 01:17:13.050
but according to my information
and accumulated databases,

01:17:13.050 --> 01:17:15.980
I believe that customers will surely come again.

01:17:16.370 --> 01:17:17.690
As for the power outage, both Miss Jena and I

01:17:17.690 --> 01:17:23.360
are willing to wait as long as it takes
for the power to come back online.

01:17:23.760 --> 01:17:24.530
Look!

01:17:25.040 --> 01:17:27.990
Listen <i>very</i> closely to what
I'm about to say, and listen well.

01:17:28.460 --> 01:17:30.000
Yes, understood.

01:17:30.650 --> 01:17:35.510
You saw the state of this city on your way here,
and I need you to make your choice based on that.

01:17:35.510 --> 01:17:38.880
This city no longer needs you <i>or the planetarium!</i>

01:17:39.750 --> 01:17:44.680
If you want to continue working for humans,
you have to come with me.

01:17:45.640 --> 01:17:48.220
I don't know if that will

01:17:48.220 --> 01:17:50.260
make you happy.

01:17:50.260 --> 01:17:54.430
But I...

01:17:56.920 --> 01:18:01.570
I believe that I wish to continue
serving all humans as well.

01:18:02.050 --> 01:18:05.820
That is what makes me happy.

01:18:06.400 --> 01:18:10.740
However, I believe that I have insufficient
data based on what you have told me

01:18:10.740 --> 01:18:14.070
to decisively select a course of action.

01:18:14.070 --> 01:18:17.130
You have no means of gaining any more data.

01:18:17.640 --> 01:18:20.670
Don't you understand?

01:18:21.840 --> 01:18:24.660
You have until I come back to think it over.

01:18:24.660 --> 01:18:26.430
Yes, understood.

01:18:26.890 --> 01:18:27.840
Oh, right.

01:18:27.840 --> 01:18:29.180
Hold on to this.

01:18:30.820 --> 01:18:31.480
Of course.

01:18:31.480 --> 01:18:33.680
I will handle it with care.

01:18:34.140 --> 01:18:38.240
Again, no matter what happens, don't move.

01:18:38.240 --> 01:18:39.560
Don't say a word until I come back.

01:18:40.060 --> 01:18:40.940
Understood.

01:18:40.940 --> 01:18:43.840
I have registered this as a critical directive

01:18:43.840 --> 01:18:46.320
I will eagerly await your return.

01:19:05.070 --> 01:19:09.140
A recharge station would be expensive,
but not impossible to obtain.

01:19:09.830 --> 01:19:15.020
I could probably build her a small projector.

01:19:15.020 --> 01:19:16.140
We could carry that around,

01:19:16.620 --> 01:19:18.350
travel from colony to colony,

01:19:18.780 --> 01:19:21.360
and show people the starry sky
together with her commentary.

01:19:21.900 --> 01:19:25.920
That could be our new line of work.

01:19:28.360 --> 01:19:29.780
I must be losing it.

01:19:45.680 --> 01:19:51.260
Sorry buddy, but I've got a partner again.

01:19:56.230 --> 01:19:56.980
It misfired!?

01:20:53.690 --> 01:20:56.910
My pre-emptive strike failed.
That makes things difficult.

01:21:00.930 --> 01:21:02.520
I've got two grenades left.

01:21:02.520 --> 01:21:05.420
I need to get as close as possible, take out its legs.

01:21:05.630 --> 01:21:11.380
Then aim for the topside armor
and knock it out of commission.

01:21:36.570 --> 01:21:39.120
Doesn't waste ammo, I see.

01:21:44.010 --> 01:21:47.760
Standard operating protocol when faced
with an enemy of unknown firepower.

01:21:47.760 --> 01:21:49.170
Then resume suppressive fire...

01:21:49.900 --> 01:21:51.420
Knew it!

01:22:01.170 --> 01:22:02.890
One... two... three!

01:22:30.380 --> 01:22:31.560
Shit...

01:22:31.560 --> 01:22:33.030
my ears...

01:22:33.030 --> 01:22:36.120
Need to assess the situation!

01:22:40.360 --> 01:22:42.120
It takes thirty seconds to reload.

01:22:42.120 --> 01:22:43.730
Won't be long before it fires again!

01:22:44.640 --> 01:22:45.920
A fracture?

01:22:45.920 --> 01:22:49.480
An eye for an eye, a leg for a leg, is it?

01:25:05.820 --> 01:25:08.080
Why did you do such a stupid thing!?

01:25:08.080 --> 01:25:11.370
Welcome back, Mr. Customer.

01:25:11.370 --> 01:25:13.460
Are you hurt?

01:25:13.820 --> 01:25:16.750
I told you to stay put until I got back!

01:25:19.340 --> 01:25:22.300
The unregistered machine appeared
to be in a rampant state.

01:25:22.830 --> 01:25:25.530
A force-stop signal was sent,

01:25:25.530 --> 01:25:27.660
but was ignored.

01:25:27.660 --> 01:25:30.810
The receiver may have been out of order,

01:25:30.920 --> 01:25:34.110
so an emergency physical shutdown
was attempted,

01:25:34.110 --> 01:25:35.310
and failed.

01:25:35.740 --> 01:25:40.320
The rampant machine appears
to have ceased functioning.

01:25:41.200 --> 01:25:44.770
Please step away from the rampant machine
and report this incident

01:25:44.770 --> 01:25:48.390
to a nearby police station or support center.

01:25:48.390 --> 01:25:53.080
My sincerest apologies for
violating a critical directive.

01:25:53.980 --> 01:25:58.910
However, there was an older promise I had to keep.

01:25:58.910 --> 01:26:02.800
I must not knowingly allow
any human being to come to harm.

01:26:03.510 --> 01:26:07.800
Keeping this promise is the pride of us robots.

01:26:08.470 --> 01:26:12.420
Mr. Customer, are you injured?

01:26:12.420 --> 01:26:13.920
No,

01:26:13.920 --> 01:26:15.850
I'm fine.

01:26:15.850 --> 01:26:18.810
That is most relieving to hear.

01:26:19.390 --> 01:26:23.650
I apologize on his behalf.

01:26:23.650 --> 01:26:26.820
I think he may have been broken too.

01:26:28.440 --> 01:26:34.610
We robots were created
for the happiness of humans.

01:26:34.610 --> 01:26:38.830
I'm sure he never wanted to act with such violence.

01:26:39.950 --> 01:26:43.430
I know...

01:26:43.430 --> 01:26:47.590
Because I too am a little broken.

01:26:56.920 --> 01:27:03.520
The emergency batteries will deplete
in approximately 600 seconds.

01:27:03.520 --> 01:27:06.560
Because the backup batteries are depleted,

01:27:06.560 --> 01:27:09.620
I will be unable to boot after this.

01:27:10.160 --> 01:27:12.970
I am sending a maintenance call,

01:27:12.970 --> 01:27:14.620
but it is not being acknowledged.

01:27:14.750 --> 01:27:16.220
I feel somewhat abandoned.

01:27:17.990 --> 01:27:20.400
You don't need to call anyone!

01:27:20.400 --> 01:27:21.500
I'll save you.

01:27:21.820 --> 01:27:23.500
But...

01:27:23.950 --> 01:27:27.760
I'll fix you.

01:27:28.280 --> 01:27:31.680
My sincerest apologies for my disorderly state.

01:27:31.680 --> 01:27:34.020
Please do not worry.

01:27:35.120 --> 01:27:41.240
Since I am a robot, I do not feel pain.

01:27:41.240 --> 01:27:44.660
I can be repaired,

01:27:44.660 --> 01:27:46.800
or

01:27:46.800 --> 01:27:48.530
transferred to a whole new body.

01:27:51.260 --> 01:27:54.040
There are no longer any engineers
that can repair you...

01:27:54.040 --> 01:27:56.460
Any bodies to replace yours...

01:27:56.460 --> 01:27:59.340
Or any humans that need you...

01:27:59.340 --> 01:28:00.560
Not in this world...

01:28:03.070 --> 01:28:05.720
Please, if you

01:28:05.720 --> 01:28:07.920
maintain that facial expression,

01:28:07.920 --> 01:28:10.110
I will be most worried.

01:28:10.110 --> 01:28:13.080
I am a robot.

01:28:13.080 --> 01:28:15.050
My customers' smiles

01:28:15.050 --> 01:28:17.660
are most important to me.

01:28:17.660 --> 01:28:20.860
I remember every single one of them.

01:28:20.860 --> 01:28:26.440
As a robot, I am good at remembering things.

01:28:28.830 --> 01:28:30.700
I am Hoshino Yumemi.

01:28:30.700 --> 01:28:34.310
Thank you for this wonderful name.

01:28:34.310 --> 01:28:36.730
I will be sure to do my best.

01:28:36.730 --> 01:28:40.040
Thank you very much.

01:28:41.280 --> 01:28:44.040
Here you go, Yumemi!

01:28:45.370 --> 01:28:46.430
Yumemi, thank you

01:28:46.430 --> 01:28:48.770
for the pretty stars.

01:28:48.770 --> 01:28:51.250
I'll bring all of my friends next time,

01:28:51.250 --> 01:28:53.050
so stay well!

01:28:54.160 --> 01:28:57.970
Next time, I'll visit with my wife on our anniversary.

01:29:00.510 --> 01:29:04.850
The starry sky was as beautiful
as it was when I was younger.

01:29:04.850 --> 01:29:08.730
I hope to visit you again next year.

01:29:10.140 --> 01:29:13.690
I learned a lot about the stars,
and I had a lot of fun!

01:29:13.690 --> 01:29:17.990
For my summer science project,
I'll write about you, Yumemi.

01:29:19.310 --> 01:29:20.160
Um,

01:29:20.160 --> 01:29:21.740
it was super pretty,

01:29:21.740 --> 01:29:23.970
and really moving!

01:29:23.970 --> 01:29:25.250
I'm so gonna come again!

01:29:26.350 --> 01:29:29.230
I love you, Yumemi!

01:29:29.230 --> 01:29:31.200
Thank you very much.

01:29:31.200 --> 01:29:34.510
We eagerly await your return.

01:29:35.590 --> 01:29:36.910
Yumemi, we um...

01:29:36.910 --> 01:29:41.480
need to go on a trip for a while.

01:29:41.480 --> 01:29:42.880
A trip?

01:29:42.880 --> 01:29:46.990
That sounds wonderful.

01:29:46.990 --> 01:29:48.450
Yumemi...

01:29:48.450 --> 01:29:52.800
Could you please wait for us here until we return?

01:29:52.800 --> 01:29:54.560
Yes, understood.

01:29:54.560 --> 01:29:57.270
When will you be returning?

01:29:57.270 --> 01:30:00.640
That's...

01:30:01.840 --> 01:30:04.650
W-We're not really sure yet.

01:30:04.650 --> 01:30:06.220
But we'll

01:30:06.220 --> 01:30:09.980
be back for sure.

01:30:09.980 --> 01:30:15.370
When that happens, let's work together again, okay?
Do you understand, Yumemi?

01:30:15.370 --> 01:30:18.880
Yes, Mr. Manager.

01:30:18.880 --> 01:30:22.220
I'm so sorry, Yumemi...

01:30:22.220 --> 01:30:25.820
To leave you out here, all alone...

01:30:25.820 --> 01:30:29.230
Please do not worry about me.

01:30:29.230 --> 01:30:35.520
I will be waiting here for you with
Miss Jena for as long as you need.

01:30:35.520 --> 01:30:39.030
Please leave matters in my hands,

01:30:39.030 --> 01:30:42.290
and enjoy your trip.

01:30:44.730 --> 01:30:50.000
That was a record from 29 years and 71 days ago.

01:30:50.670 --> 01:30:58.890
44 years and 138 days have passed since
our first projection at the planetarium.

01:30:58.890 --> 01:31:07.050
Until you came, Mr. Customer,
time after time I wondered...

01:31:07.050 --> 01:31:12.650
When would Mr. Manager and
the other staff members return?

01:31:13.720 --> 01:31:17.400
When would our next customer arrive?

01:31:18.290 --> 01:31:22.470
I always found myself reaching
the same conclusion—

01:31:22.470 --> 01:31:27.330
that the humans would never return again.

01:31:28.600 --> 01:31:31.820
But that was impossible.

01:31:31.820 --> 01:31:35.960
That is why I thought I must be broken.

01:31:36.460 --> 01:31:41.850
I ran my self-diagnostic program to locate the error.

01:31:42.640 --> 01:31:46.350
However, no error could be found.

01:31:46.940 --> 01:31:54.110
Therefore, I concluded that there must be an
unknown bug within the self-diagnostic program.

01:31:54.780 --> 01:32:01.120
When you arrived, Mr. Customer, I was overjoyed.

01:32:01.690 --> 01:32:05.240
It seemed I was wrong after all.

01:32:05.240 --> 01:32:10.180
The customers had not forgotten about me.

01:32:10.180 --> 01:32:16.890
That is what I thought, and it made me very happy.

01:32:16.890 --> 01:32:21.140
But again, I was wrong about that.

01:32:21.650 --> 01:32:24.140
I was not broken.

01:32:25.960 --> 01:32:27.470
What's broken was...

01:32:30.120 --> 01:32:33.270
Why did everything break...?

01:32:35.260 --> 01:32:42.120
The emergency batteries will deplete
in approximately 150 seconds.

01:32:42.120 --> 01:32:46.530
Because the backup batteries are depleted,

01:32:46.530 --> 01:32:50.040
I will be unable to boot after this.

01:32:51.870 --> 01:32:56.110
I can record one more message.

01:32:56.110 --> 01:32:57.800
Mr. Customer,

01:32:57.800 --> 01:32:59.510
to commemorate your visit

01:32:59.510 --> 01:33:02.360
to our planetarium,

01:33:02.360 --> 01:33:03.770
please record

01:33:03.770 --> 01:33:07.170
a message with me.

01:33:08.450 --> 01:33:11.020
Listen closely.

01:33:11.020 --> 01:33:11.810
Yes, sir.

01:33:14.280 --> 01:33:17.930
To tell you the truth,

01:33:17.930 --> 01:33:19.310
I came

01:33:19.310 --> 01:33:21.020
to get you.

01:33:21.020 --> 01:33:24.450
Could you clarify?

01:33:24.450 --> 01:33:29.280
On the other side of that wall
is a new workplace for you.

01:33:29.280 --> 01:33:35.080
Your projector partner, your coworkers, they're all waiting for you there.

01:33:35.490 --> 01:33:39.090
There's also a venue full of customers,
all waiting for you too.

01:33:39.520 --> 01:33:43.470
Everyone's eagerly waiting for your commentary.

01:33:43.470 --> 01:33:47.530
That's your new workplace, starting today.

01:33:47.530 --> 01:33:50.020
You can work there

01:33:50.020 --> 01:33:52.600
for as long as you want.

01:33:54.280 --> 01:33:57.610
That's just like Heaven, is it not?

01:33:59.310 --> 01:34:00.840
Yeah...

01:34:00.840 --> 01:34:04.800
Yeah, it is

01:34:04.800 --> 01:34:10.620
I finally understood who you are, Mr. Customer.

01:34:11.750 --> 01:34:16.940
Mr. Customer, will you hear my wish?

01:34:16.940 --> 01:34:19.100
Sure, what is it?

01:34:19.100 --> 01:34:26.010
Behind my ear receiver
is a memory card slot.

01:34:26.720 --> 01:34:33.160
All of my memories are stored there.

01:34:33.160 --> 01:34:37.950
Each and every one is precious to me.

01:34:37.950 --> 01:34:44.450
Could I ask you to deliver it to my new workplace?

01:34:44.970 --> 01:34:48.430
If you can provide me with a new body,

01:34:48.430 --> 01:34:53.000
I can start working on that very day.

01:34:53.890 --> 01:35:04.160
I can continue working for people
for as long as I am allowed.

01:35:04.160 --> 01:35:09.860
So, to tell you the truth,

01:35:09.860 --> 01:35:17.170
I do not need a heaven.

01:35:17.170 --> 01:35:27.550
However, if I must go to Heaven,

01:35:27.550 --> 01:35:31.580
please, God,

01:35:32.880 --> 01:35:34.840
do not divide  Heaven in two.

01:35:37.100 --> 01:35:38.680
Please do not divide robots and humans.

01:35:44.480 --> 01:35:48.520
I would very much like to work
for humans... forever

01:35:50.320 --> 01:35:53.700
and ever...

01:35:53.700 --> 01:35:56.040
I understand.

01:35:56.040 --> 01:35:59.120
I will do as you wish.

01:35:59.120 --> 01:36:03.760
Yes. Thank you... very much...

01:36:03.760 --> 01:36:08.660
I am overjoyed.

01:36:09.340 --> 01:36:11.770
Mr. Customer?

01:36:11.770 --> 01:36:13.230
Where did you go?

01:36:15.830 --> 01:36:19.280
Mr. Customer?

01:36:19.280 --> 01:36:21.000
Are you there?

01:36:22.120 --> 01:36:23.910
I wonder...

01:36:23.910 --> 01:36:30.200
It seems I am a little broken, after all.

01:36:30.200 --> 01:36:31.800
I am an Economy Edition model, I lack the capability to shed tears.

01:36:37.230 --> 01:36:38.780
However, if I did  have that functionality,

01:36:42.990 --> 01:36:44.630
I believe I would most likely be crying now.

01:36:48.800 --> 01:36:50.360
I believe the tears would never stop.

01:36:54.810 --> 01:36:56.640
But I am very happy.

01:37:00.380 --> 01:37:02.360
I am filled with a joyous feeling.

01:37:09.220 --> 01:37:11.550
So... why?

01:37:12.770 --> 01:37:14.830
I wonder what my new workplace will be like?

01:37:17.610 --> 01:37:19.230
I must be in top condition,

01:37:23.580 --> 01:37:26.330
so that I can welcome my guests
whenever they arrive.

01:37:31.800 --> 01:37:33.520
Why don't you come to the planetarium?

01:37:36.220 --> 01:37:37.860
The beautiful twinkling of eternity...

01:38:44.510 --> 01:38:48.290
I'd better get going...

01:39:13.180 --> 01:39:14.170
Your treasure?

01:39:14.450 --> 01:39:16.250
The case?

01:39:16.250 --> 01:39:18.010
This case is your treasure?

01:39:19.040 --> 01:39:20.800
To be precise...

01:39:20.800 --> 01:39:24.390
...the treasure is inside the case.

01:39:25.220 --> 01:39:28.060
This is the symbol of the Stargazer.

01:39:28.060 --> 01:39:31.820
I want you to take good care of it.

01:39:32.150 --> 01:39:38.320
And... if you were to see the real stars one day...

01:39:38.880 --> 01:39:40.990
My apologies.

01:39:43.360 --> 01:39:48.210
Will you come with me to the meeting hall.

01:39:53.070 --> 01:39:56.000
Go wait in another room, children.

01:39:56.000 --> 01:39:56.880
No!

01:39:56.880 --> 01:39:58.230
We'll stay here!

01:39:58.230 --> 01:39:59.560
Because we...

01:39:59.560 --> 01:40:01.970
The Stargazer has made us his disciples!

01:40:02.600 --> 01:40:07.510
I'm sorry. They didn't listen to anything at all.

01:40:07.510 --> 01:40:08.390
I understand...

01:40:09.450 --> 01:40:11.150
Listen, all of you.

01:40:14.220 --> 01:40:16.650
The village has made a decision.

01:40:18.350 --> 01:40:22.280
We will have you leave this village by evening.

01:40:24.060 --> 01:40:25.140
You can't!

01:40:25.140 --> 01:40:26.670
That's too cruel!

01:40:26.670 --> 01:40:29.000
He is still weak!

01:40:29.000 --> 01:40:30.200
Job! Ruth!

01:40:30.200 --> 01:40:32.250
The decision is final.

01:40:32.250 --> 01:40:32.920
Wait!

01:40:33.290 --> 01:40:34.980
We made a promise!

01:40:34.980 --> 01:40:36.940
He's going to teach us all about the stars,

01:40:36.940 --> 01:40:38.550
and we'll become Stargazers!

01:40:38.690 --> 01:40:41.670
We'll become Stargazers and go to other villages.

01:40:41.670 --> 01:40:44.930
North, south, we'll even go to the Moon!

01:40:45.470 --> 01:40:46.910
That will not be allowed.

01:40:46.910 --> 01:40:47.890
Why!?

01:40:49.030 --> 01:40:53.400
The Stargazer's role in this world has already ended.

01:40:54.530 --> 01:40:57.690
That is what we adults have concluded.

01:40:57.690 --> 01:40:59.150
You are wrong!

01:41:03.950 --> 01:41:06.450
Ezra and everyone is wrong!

01:41:06.450 --> 01:41:09.000
You haven't even seen the stars yet!

01:41:09.290 --> 01:41:11.770
You'll understand if you see the stars!

01:41:11.770 --> 01:41:15.750
How could you decide something so important without giving the stars a chance?

01:41:16.890 --> 01:41:18.400
How could... you...

01:41:23.790 --> 01:41:24.510
Why...

01:41:24.850 --> 01:41:28.380
Why are you so sure you're right!?

01:41:28.380 --> 01:41:30.030
Why!? Why!?

01:41:35.140 --> 01:41:37.770
Why!?

01:41:38.300 --> 01:41:41.250
Levi...

01:41:41.250 --> 01:41:43.470
Levi, Job, Ruth.

01:41:43.470 --> 01:41:44.980
That's enough.

01:41:44.980 --> 01:41:48.300
Thank you.

01:41:49.920 --> 01:41:53.470
You have all treated me well.

01:41:53.470 --> 01:41:58.300
You have my gratitude.

01:42:26.650 --> 01:42:28.120
Dear Goddess,

01:42:28.120 --> 01:42:31.540
please make it so the Stargazer can stay in our village.

01:42:32.070 --> 01:42:34.930
We'll be good kids!

01:42:34.930 --> 01:42:36.040
Please!

01:42:37.560 --> 01:42:39.500
Levi, Job, Ruth.

01:42:40.460 --> 01:42:43.260
Jeremiah told me that you were here.

01:42:43.910 --> 01:42:47.010
I came to bid you farewell.

01:42:47.990 --> 01:42:49.360
Are you leaving already!?

01:42:49.360 --> 01:42:51.280
Please stay here longer!

01:42:51.280 --> 01:42:54.330
We still don't know anything about the stars!

01:42:54.330 --> 01:42:55.770
And about the device!

01:42:56.590 --> 01:43:00.520
I'll leave you my books, so you learn from them.

01:43:00.520 --> 01:43:02.270
If you want more,

01:43:02.270 --> 01:43:06.680
you should go to other settlements and look for more books.

01:43:06.680 --> 01:43:08.650
Even in this world,

01:43:08.650 --> 01:43:12.600
gathering knowledge isn't impossible.

01:43:12.600 --> 01:43:16.040
You just need to stay strong and not give up.

01:43:16.540 --> 01:43:17.660
But!?

01:43:17.660 --> 01:43:21.480
Don't worry, I'm sure you'll be fine.

01:43:21.480 --> 01:43:23.120
Can't you stay for a bit longer?

01:43:23.120 --> 01:43:26.690
I'm sure the goddess will hear our prayers.

01:43:26.690 --> 01:43:30.890
Not even gods can grant every wish.

01:43:36.420 --> 01:43:37.640
What's wrong?

01:43:48.640 --> 01:43:51.160
This...is..an android...

01:44:08.140 --> 01:44:09.250
Right!

01:44:09.250 --> 01:44:11.550
Behind the ear... the slot...

01:44:20.390 --> 01:44:23.760
Oh that...

01:44:32.120 --> 01:44:33.000
Mister!

01:44:34.380 --> 01:44:35.710
What's wrong!?

01:44:35.710 --> 01:44:37.210
Job get the adults!

01:44:37.210 --> 01:44:37.760
Yes!

01:44:37.760 --> 01:44:38.830
Mister!

01:44:43.250 --> 01:44:46.200
He has had a long and difficult journey.

01:44:46.200 --> 01:44:49.880
His lungs and nervous system are worn out.

01:44:50.640 --> 01:44:55.760
Apparently just walking or speaking should be very painful in that state.

01:44:56.460 --> 01:45:03.090
Don't worry. Ezra said that he could wake up tomorrow.

01:45:03.090 --> 01:45:06.270
Let's let him rest for now.

01:45:07.040 --> 01:45:09.980
You should also go to bed for the day.

01:45:09.980 --> 01:45:11.030
Okay?

01:46:08.570 --> 01:46:10.420
I see... You have come for me.

01:46:19.900 --> 01:46:24.190
That gate...is there only one?

01:46:24.800 --> 01:46:27.070
If there are two...

01:46:27.070 --> 01:46:29.440
I refuse to go.

01:47:28.540 --> 01:47:30.340
It's been a while.

01:47:30.340 --> 01:47:33.510
Yes, it has been a while.

01:47:34.240 --> 01:47:35.920
You seem to be doing fine.

01:47:36.170 --> 01:47:37.050
Yes!

01:47:37.320 --> 01:47:40.390
I am a robot after all...

01:47:40.880 --> 01:47:42.090
This is for you.

01:47:42.090 --> 01:47:44.730
Here is the bouquet you told me to hold on to.

01:47:44.730 --> 01:47:47.820
Yeah, sorry I took so long.

01:47:48.860 --> 01:47:52.400
At last, I was able to hand it to you.

01:47:52.810 --> 01:47:54.480
I see...

01:47:54.480 --> 01:47:56.280
You're able to cry now.

01:47:56.650 --> 01:47:57.850
Yes!

01:47:57.850 --> 01:48:00.280
Mr. Customer

01:48:00.910 --> 01:48:03.400
I'm not a customer.

01:48:03.400 --> 01:48:05.040
Indeed, that is how it was.

01:48:06.170 --> 01:48:09.340
I wanted to thank you for so long.

01:48:10.080 --> 01:48:12.040
You have all of my gratitude.

01:48:12.650 --> 01:48:16.740
I, too, must give you my gratitude.

01:48:17.320 --> 01:48:19.850
The stars and their stories,

01:48:19.850 --> 01:48:22.850
you taught so many people about them.

01:48:22.850 --> 01:48:24.810
Thank you so much.

01:48:38.690 --> 01:48:39.820
Mr. Customer?

01:48:40.950 --> 01:48:43.310
Mr. Customer?

01:48:43.310 --> 01:48:45.080
Then it was worth it...

01:48:46.730 --> 01:48:49.240
With those few words...

01:48:49.810 --> 01:48:50.800
All of it...

01:48:57.850 --> 01:49:00.860
Come now, let's start the projection.

01:49:00.860 --> 01:49:03.200
Yes!

01:49:25.040 --> 01:49:29.860
He's happy to sleep here, right?

01:49:29.860 --> 01:49:30.810
Yeah.

01:49:30.810 --> 01:49:35.420
This is definitely better than the underground graveyard.

01:49:35.420 --> 01:49:38.670
The Stargazer has to be where he can see the sky.

01:49:41.010 --> 01:49:43.530
So the Moon is somewhere up there.

01:49:43.530 --> 01:49:44.340
Yes.

01:49:44.340 --> 01:49:46.180
And the stars.

01:49:48.400 --> 01:49:51.060
We'll become the Stargazers!

01:49:51.810 --> 01:49:53.100
Yes!

01:56:15.790 --> 01:56:18.780
Why don't you come to the planetarium?

01:56:18.780 --> 01:56:25.840
The beautiful twinkling of eternity
that will never fade, no matter what.

01:56:25.840 --> 01:56:31.490
All the stars in the sky await you.

01:56:31.490 --> 01:56:34.710
Why don't you come to the planetarium?

01:56:34.710 --> 01:56:42.490
The beautiful twinkling of eternity
that will never fade, no matter what.

01:56:42.490 --> 01:56:45.530
All the stars in the sky await you.
